{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along","id":851941,"title":"What if Abyssals were fighting Oblivion all along?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-23T12:53:30-07:00","id":851941,"title":"What if Abyssals were fighting Oblivion all along?","content":"So this is just a story idea I'd like to workshop, not in any way a suggestion for the next edition of Abyssal Exalted or Exalted canon in general,<br /> <br /> But what if most Deathknights were actively working to <i>subvert</i> Oblivion by ensuring a steady stream of souls into the Underworld? In 2nd ed Stygia was a First Age project to bind Oblivion and ensure that it never swallowed Creation whole by using ghosts as stabilizing elements. Taking that an extra step, I have this notion that Deathknights might spread death and misery in Creation in order to ensure that enough ghosts enter the afterlife to keep the Maw from spreading.<br /> <br /> This would most likely be little understood by the living people they terrorize, and it's not to their benefit to be forthcoming with their reasoning. The end result would be Deathknights that on the surface seem like heartless abominations prowling Creation for hapless victims, but who's actions can be at least partially justified by the fact that if they <i>don't </i>do this, Oblivion may grow and bring final death to all things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-23-2016, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:00:53-07:00","id":851945,"title":"","content":"&quot;Power hath descended forth from thy hand, that our feet may swiftly carry out thy command. So we shall flow a river forth to thee, and teeming with souls shall it ever be.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a cool idea, and the Deathlords could even be encouraging it, because they like actually doing things versus just not existing, despite what their masters may appear to be on about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:22:16-07:00","id":851961,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting thought, and the known notions of the Chivalry Of Death actually strike me as possibly very explicable by the suggestion.<br /> <br /> From what we've learned, the instinctual &quot;code&quot; of the Abyssals is obtuse to the living, even patiently explained, and it seems to push furthering the place of death (as opposed to eternal non-existence) in the world and maximizing that which is resonant to it, as a waymark for the deathknights to spread the order of the grave as its Lawgivers. It might even be interpreted as promoting a certain permanence to death as a part of Creation, which doubles as an anchor for the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-23-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:27:38-07:00","id":851971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=851945#post851945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Power hath descended forth from thy hand, that our feet may swiftly carry out thy command. So we shall flow a river forth to thee, and teeming with souls shall it ever be.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a cool idea, and the Deathlords could even be encouraging it, because they like actually doing things versus just not existing, despite what their masters may appear to be on about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man that is <i>such </i>a great quote for this. If this <i>was</i> part of a book I'd want that on the chapter preface.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Deathlords being very split on this mission statement, as they were on the &quot;kill everything&quot; mission statement of canon 2nd ed. Some might be fully on board but paying lip service to the idea that they need more souls to power the increasingly nonsensical war machines they &quot;eventually&quot; plan to roll over Creation with. Some might actively subvert the notion and be abominations in the Underworld, responsible for mass genocides of ghostly populations. Still others might be so far gone that they don't consistently support or oppose it, but vacillate wildly depending on circumstances. I personally imagine a Creation-based oblivion loyalist who styles themselves as a master exorcist and recruits Creation powers like the Solar exalted to help them &quot;cleanse&quot; the Underworld, not knowing that they actually further oblivion's cause in doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T21:01:24-07:00","id":852221,"title":"","content":"The maw of Oblivion widens with every ghost that falls into it; indeed, out of the people that have fallen into Oblivion, the <i>overwhelmingly vast majority</i> have been ghosts.<br /> <br /> Creating more ghosts thus creates more people who <i>can</i> fall into Oblivion (and thus advance its approach). Absent the sort of infrastructure present in the First Age, adding a shitload of numbers isn't going to help, and may only make things worse!<br /> <br /> (In a sense, it's like adding ten thousand people to an army, without giving them any training or weapons or food or other supplies, when the army already has so little to spare that they're eating shoe leather and fighting with broken swords. Except also they're fighting zombies or something, where every kill on the part of the enemies swells their rank.)<br /> <br /> I suspect that the Solars of the First Age influenced ghostly society the way they did because the ghosts were already<i> there</i>, not because ghosts are super-effective at sealing away the encroaching Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-24-2016, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T21:19:06-07:00","id":852232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852221#post852221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect that the Solars of the First Age influenced ghostly society the way they did because the ghosts were already<i> there</i>, not because ghosts are super-effective at sealing away the encroaching Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suspect, hell; in 2e this was made explicit. The Solar Deliberative was like &quot;well, we don't actually know how to get rid of the Underworld, and conducting a ghost genocide seems difficult and possibly counter-productive, so... yeah.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T22:14:45-07:00","id":852245,"title":"","content":"This is a really interesting idea. I really hope 3E explores it. I never felt that ghosts quite got their due in the past books and would like to see more inspiration like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T22:15:09-07:00","id":852247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852221#post852221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The maw of Oblivion widens with every ghost that falls into it; indeed, out of the people that have fallen into Oblivion, the <i>overwhelmingly vast majority</i> have been ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure which part of 2e canon you are citing here, but my sincere impression was that the Maw grows when there are fewer ghosts present to stop it. It doesn't &quot;feed&quot; on ghosts, and if that were the case the most effective means of expediting total extinction would be to push all of Stygia into it at spear point which the Death Lords are more than capable of doing in 2e. In fact, I can't think of a single example of a Deathlord in 2e canon that sacrifices ghosts to Oblivion for any reason other than scare tactics or twisted amusement. So you can rule that in your game if you like, but it has some pretty serious balance and plot issues I would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T22:19:46-07:00","id":852250,"title":"","content":"The idea is older than 2e (older even than Exalted, dating all the way back to its origins in <i>Wraith</i>), but it gets a mention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T03:57:00-07:00","id":852316,"title":"","content":"Insofar as I care for Oblivion at all, I think its concept is diminished somewhat if it amounts to an Underworld version of the Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:03:03-07:00","id":852319,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, I just searched the backer PDF for &quot;oblivion&quot;, and noticed two things:<br /> <br /> 1. It is mentioned only a handful of time throughout the whole book, which may not be that weird or telling (it's hardly the most important thing to talk about in the core), and<br /> 2. It's never capitalized in the text. It's always oblivion, never Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder how important a concept it's actually going to be this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:19:28-07:00","id":852322,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cIn the mirrors of the many judgments, my hands are the color of blood. I sometimes fancy myself an evil which exists to oppose other evils; and on that great Day of which the prophets speak but in which they do not truly believe, on the day the world is utterly cleansed of evil, then I too will go down into darkness, swallowing curses. Until then, I will not wash my hands nor let them hang useless.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <br /> In a game I ran, Oblivion was undefined and Abyssals were unknown to them, in a great philosophical war to define what it IS and what it IS NOT. I'm reminded of the idea that to have a chance of power over a spirit, first you must give its name... even if you must make it have a name so you can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T06:08:07-07:00","id":852365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852245#post852245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really interesting idea. I really hope 3E explores it. I never felt that ghosts quite got their due in the past books and would like to see more inspiration like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this idea singlehandedly justified Abyssals being a playable splat to me (versus just the OWoD-ish approach to make things better suited as NPCs playable at some point), so it's now my headcanon, though I somewhat doubt 3e will take &quot;knight of the dead&quot; to these sort of lengths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-24-2016, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T09:21:30-07:00","id":852452,"title":"","content":"The 3E core makes several references to the Abyssals as &quot;Death's Lawgivers&quot; which is something new. I am hopeful that this reflects a more interesting approach to their role in the setting than we've seen, and not just a trite reference to being the gothy Solar knockoffs we've had up to now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T12:53:05-07:00","id":852548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=851945#post851945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Power hath descended forth from thy hand, that our feet may swiftly carry out thy command. So we shall flow a river forth to thee, and teeming with souls shall it ever be.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Boondock. Saints.<br /> (Hellsing Abridged: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=kn4QfCjdESM\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=kn4QfCjdESM</a> 3:06-4:00)<br /> <br /> <br /> It could make for a good reveal that &quot;maybe Abyssals aren't so bad!&quot; But they're still killing people in Creation. It's kind of black and gray morality. &quot;Do we sacrifice a bunch of people so the world can go on another day?&quot; I really don't like it when you think much past the surface.<br /> <br /> That said, combines great with the idea I've heard that the Deathlords robbed the tombs of the sleeping Neverborn to get their powers, with the Neverborn holding no control over them. The Deathlords can actually be the GOOD GUYS, culling people in Creation to ensure its continued survival! &quot;For the greater good.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe the Great Contagion was necessary, as Oblivion was about to eat everything. It stopped when it did because it was SUPPOSED TO. The Scarlet Empress gained access to the Sword of Creation because a Solar Ghost Deathlord passed it on to her so she could save Creation from the unfortunate side-effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 03-24-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:29:00-07:00","id":852566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852548#post852548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Scarlet Empress gained access to the Sword of Creation because a Solar Ghost Deathlord passed it on to her so she could save Creation from the unfortunate side-effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool idea up til this point. The Empress's action hero bit shouldn't be retconned to &quot;because a Solar let her.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:30:01-07:00","id":852567,"title":"","content":"Esoteric metaphysical justification for concretely bad behavior always strikes me as weaksauce bullshit whenever fantasy fiction authors invoke it for why their bad boys aren't <i>actually</i> bad after all and so the audience doesn't have to feel guilty for liking them. And that's what this sort of thing always amounts to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:39:40-07:00","id":852572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852567#post852567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esoteric metaphysical justification for concretely bad behavior always strikes me as weaksauce bullshit whenever fantasy fiction authors invoke it for why their bad boys aren't <i>actually</i> bad after all and so the audience doesn't have to feel guilty for liking them. And that's what this sort of thing always amounts to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas that I have but one 'Like' to give.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:10:06-07:00","id":852587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852548#post852548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, combines great with the idea I've heard that the Deathlords robbed the tombs of the sleeping Neverborn to get their powers, with the Neverborn holding no control over them. The Deathlords can actually be the GOOD GUYS, culling people in Creation to ensure its continued survival! &quot;For the greater good.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Deathlord Good Guys, but I also want at least one deathlord to be &quot;doing the will of the Neverborn&quot; (Now whether they are crazy or actually doing the will of the Neverborn is up to the ST). Basically, I want a wide range of shades of dark grey for the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> I'd go more into it, but I want to use some of my ideas for my Shogunate Quest. Apparently I already said too much in other threads, because one of the comments here is mimicing my plans for the Quest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-24-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:19:57-07:00","id":852595,"title":"","content":"&quot;For the greater good&quot; in that sense and embraced wholeheartedly is and always has been satire. There's a reason why it's best known from Warhammer 40k and Hot Fuzz. Also, moving the Deathlords from &quot;Servants of the Neverborn&quot; to &quot;Free actors who stole power from the Neverborn&quot; does not move them from selfish to altruistic without significantly more alteration necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:26:17-07:00","id":852599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852595#post852595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;For the greater good&quot; in that sense and embraced wholeheartedly is and always has been satire. There's a reason why it's best known from Warhammer 40k and Hot Fuzz. Also, moving the Deathlords from &quot;Servants of the Neverborn&quot; to &quot;Free actors who stole power from the Neverborn&quot; does not move them from selfish to altruistic without significantly more alteration necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe &quot;good guys&quot; is too strong of a term. I'd like Deathlords to be morally grey enough for characters to make bargains and deals with them without looking like idiots or evil for doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:27:09-07:00","id":852601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852548#post852548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Deathlords can actually be the GOOD GUYS, culling people in Creation to ensure its continued survival! &quot;For the greater good.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The greater good.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:51:29-07:00","id":852618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852567#post852567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esoteric metaphysical justification for concretely bad behavior always strikes me as weaksauce bullshit whenever fantasy fiction authors invoke it for why their bad boys aren't <i>actually</i> bad after all and so the audience doesn't have to feel guilty for liking them. And that's what this sort of thing always amounts to.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's still recognized as bad or harmful behavior and not inherently justified because it might in addition serve a beneficial metaphysical purpose to a degree, it doesn't have to fall into that, does it?<br /> <br /> I think there's more meaningful ambiguity to the idea if it's based on an ultimately selfish rather than altruistic notion; and I could see that as something to play into evening out and diversifying the aims and beliefs of the Deathlords.That is to say, adressing the OP's idea: by spreading the resonance and essence of death through Creation and ordering it, the Abyssals strengthen the permanence of the Underworld; they solidify it and anchor the dead passions that keep its residents moving. This may hold back the oblivion at the bottom of the Deathlords' kingdoms, and it may smother the Neverborn in their dreaming deaths further. But they're still spreading death and despair through Creation and imposing the laws of the grave upon it, for effectively the direct benefit of the Underworld alone and its survival as more than a realm of mere remembrance, more filled and teeming than an ocean of dead rivers that carry ghosts to forgetfulness or reincarnation.<br /> <br /> A deathknight who rides alone may still be able to find comfort in the fact that even called by the chivalry of death, they have some place in keeping Creation too as it is, no matter how small or unnoticed in the grand scheme of things it may be. And a deathknight who serves a Deathlord may carve out a meaning and place in the Underworld or establish themselves without being by definition an actor of nihilism and a hand to oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-24-2016, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:20:20-07:00","id":852632,"title":"","content":"I think weird metaphysical justification for immoral action is a hack writing move, because the writer invents the metaphysics. You can justify a convoluted metaphysical reason for <i>anything</i> being &quot;For the greater good,&quot; up to and including the actual historical Holocaust, and if you're the writer and thus get to decide the objective, from-an-omniscient-point-of-view truth of your metaphysics, who's to gainsay you? But the reader is fully <i>aware</i> that it's all just a bunch of arbitrary bullshit you made up, and that you <i>can</i> construct a set of supernatural universal rules to any specification you desire. I know that whenever I encounter a writer who wants to paint a mass murderer as &quot;Not actually evil&quot; because handwave handwave cosmic balance, I immediately think &quot;This writer wants to incorporate mass murder into his stories but actually engaging with it in any way but the most superficial makes him uncomfortable.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Likewise, taking a character who you have painted as evil and then revealing that he's <i>actually justified</i> because handwave handwave is the kind of &quot;What a tweest!&quot; plot twist that M. Night Shamalan <i>parodies</i> get up to. M. Night Shamalan parodies and manga writers who have to justify their minor, murderous and sadistic second-act miniboss sticking around and joining the main character crew because they turned out to be popular with the audience.)<br /> <br /> If you want to make the Deathlords sympathetic in a way that fits in Creation's venue, make them selfish actors with their own agendas who are maybe, in practice, only slightly more morally compromised than all of the other awful, awful people who've risen to the top of the setting's power heap -- and then make them personally sympathetic such that they maybe have a fondness for the PCs for a personal reason, that could lead to the PCs having a fondness for them for a personal reason. Like, I'm sure y'all have heard the <i>many</i> times that I point out that the Slug engages in and promotes trafficking in sex slavery on a massive scale, and Cathak Cainan has put whole satrapies to the lash and sword and crucifix just to make examples of them to other satrapies, but nobody has a problem with those two showing up on-screen as neutral NPCs or allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 03-24-2016, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:28:27-07:00","id":852633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852632#post852632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think weird metaphysical justification for immoral action is a hack writing move, because the writer invents the metaphysics. You can justify a convoluted metaphysical reason for <i>anything</i> being &quot;For the greater good,&quot; up to and including the actual historical Holocaust, and if you're the writer and thus get to decide the objective, from-an-omniscient-point-of-view truth of your metaphysics, who's to gainsay you? But the reader is fully <i>aware</i> that it's all just a bunch of arbitrary bullshit you made up, and that you <i>can</i> construct a set of supernatural universal rules to any specification you desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for describing exactly why I dislike Madoka Magica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:29:55-07:00","id":852634,"title":"","content":"(Incidentally, from this you can probably derive why I really dislike any portrayal of the Perfect of Paragon that tries to play up &quot;But he actually really does want what's best for his people, and in practice his mass-enslaving trick really has allowed him to impose a better quality of life for the folks of Paragon than you tend to get elsewhere in Creation!&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:37:55-07:00","id":852636,"title":"","content":"&quot;In the grim darkness of the Third Age...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:48:10-07:00","id":852637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852567#post852567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esoteric metaphysical justification for concretely bad behavior always strikes me as weaksauce bullshit whenever fantasy fiction authors invoke it for why their bad boys aren't <i>actually</i> bad after all and so the audience doesn't have to feel guilty for liking them. And that's what this sort of thing always amounts to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are esoteric metaphysical justifications less legitimate a writing tool than prosaic realpolitik ones, tho?<br /> <br /> Like, the justification behind the monstrous cultural and actual genocide of the Usurpation is &quot;the Sidereals are picking the best of a bunch of really bad, high-risk options.&quot; We're never asked to just accept that it was transparently morally correct of them to do so, just that the moral calculus behind them getting their murder on is more complicated than them deciding to Usurp the Solars out of pure greed and avarice.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the setting has always encouraged us to view the Realm as having some good mixed in with all the, you know, evil Imperial bullshit they get up to. The Empress is a pretty evil tyrant, but she's also keeping the world safe the best way she knows how and trying to work with the toolset she has. The setting encourages us to consider the complexities of the situation.<br /> <br /> I don't understand why weird metaphysical stuff that poses the same questions and get to the same places are weaksauce, especially since thematically speaking, some people really like engaging with things like &quot;no, the universe actually <i>is</i> this terrible a place; it's baked in. How are you going to conduct yourself as a person given those facts?&quot;<br /> <br /> (This has occasionally gotten me in trouble, as I've had DM's had to tell me &quot;no, I will not allow your character to embark on a grand crusade to slaughter all the gods and remake the universe because you find the one they've constructed for you morally appalling. <i>This isn't that kind of game.</i>&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 03-24-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:52:45-07:00","id":852639,"title":"","content":"Prosaic realpolitik justifications for why someone is actually a good guy after all (what a tweest!) are just as bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:53:25-07:00","id":852640,"title":"","content":"It's actually possible I'm just a grumpy old man who hates plot twists for the sake of plot twists at this point, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:55:43-07:00","id":852641,"title":"","content":"A difference may be in the lack of ambiguity the idea suggests.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals may or may not have taken the right course, some are consumed by doubt and others actively regret it.<br /> <br /> Creation may fall to the Wyld if not for the dragonblooded and their Realm, or it may not.<br /> <br /> What is being proposed here, and I may be wrong about this, is that the evil acts of the Deathlords objectively contribute to the continuation of Creation, and were they to cease doing their evil shit Creation would perish.<br /> <br /> Might be it, dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:21:33-07:00","id":852649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852639#post852639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prosaic realpolitik justifications for why someone is actually a good guy after all (what a tweest!) are just as bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I was misunderstanding you, then. You're talking about narratives in which people doing crazy evil shit for good reasons <i>excuses</i> their actions, rather than narratives where that simply <i>informs</i> their actions.<br /> <br /> That's legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:37:21-07:00","id":852654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852649#post852649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh! I was misunderstanding you, then. You're talking about narratives in which people doing crazy evil shit for good reasons <i>excuses</i> their actions, rather than narratives where that simply <i>informs</i> their actions.<br /> <br /> That's legit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of people doing crazy shit for good reasons, some people may think I'm a Chejop Kejak apologist. I'm not really! I may seem sympathetic because I use him as a character in my Quest and to write him properly I got to get into his head. But that doesn't mean I think he's the good guy in the story. <br /> <br /> My preferred ending to Chejop Kejak's story is that when he dies and his ghost wakes up in the Underworld, he has to spend the rest of his undead days running away from Abyssals, Bounty Hunters and everyone else who wants his delicious five thousand year old soul for Soulsteel Forging. Ideally involving kick ass Kung Fu fights and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8yoSM9G00b0\" target=\"_blank\">Benny Hill Chase scenes</a>. <br /> <br /> /Totally posted this to inflict my mental image of Benny Hill Underworld Chase Scenes on the forum.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:41:23-07:00","id":852656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852632#post852632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to make the Deathlords sympathetic in a way that fits in Creation's venue, make them selfish actors with their own agendas who are maybe, in practice, only slightly more morally compromised than all of the other awful, awful people who've risen to the top of the setting's power heap -- and then make them personally sympathetic such that they maybe have a fondness for the PCs for a personal reason, that could lead to the PCs having a fondness for them for a personal reason. Like, I'm sure y'all have heard the <i>many</i> times that I point out that the Slug engages in and promotes trafficking in sex slavery on a massive scale, and Cathak Cainan has put whole satrapies to the lash and sword and crucifix just to make examples of them to other satrapies, but nobody has a problem with those two showing up on-screen as neutral NPCs or allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deathlords as selfishly motivated at their core and any cosmological contribution incidental to their aspirations and methods, with the effects on Creation at best minor and unobservable in normal circumstances is where I was going with that, yes. Likewise, I was going with a similar stance for the Abyssals and the chivalry of death.<br /> <br /> I didn't intend to suggest any arbitrary metaphysical explanation serve as replacement for the complexity and dubious morality that naturally come with the wide-reaching actions of powerful individuals or as a justification for horrible acts against the living or the majority of the world as it matters. At most, I was suggesting a buy-in on the part of the Deathlords that is motivated by self-interest. One which, while not forgiving of anything, could also serve as an inherent note of positive meaning to be found in existence as an Abyssal (I mean, leaving aside their potential to change the setting and do good, which shouldn't be all that much different from Solars, even if differently focused).<br /> <br /> I don't think the idea of holding back oblivion in some way should excuse or make okay anything that the Deathlords or the Abyssals do, so much as interestingly inform edges of their actions and possible motivations. To put it the way TGUEIROS mentioned the ambiguity of the Sidereal and Dragonblooded:<br /> <br /> If the Abyssals cease their march to the chivalry of death and souls stop flowing to the Deathlords' kingdoms on drums of devastation, the Underworld may eventually lose cohesion and fall into oblivion, and Creation may one day follow. Or they may not, and the shadow of death one day fill the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-24-2016, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:46:05-07:00","id":852658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852654#post852654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My preferred ending to Chejop Kejak's story is that when he dies and his ghost wakes up in the Underworld, he has to spend the rest of his undead days running away from Abyssals, Bounty Hunters and everyone else who wants his delicious five thousand year old soul for Soulsteel Forging. Ideally involving kick ass Kung Fu fights and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8yoSM9G00b0\" target=\"_blank\">Benny Hill Chase scenes</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically, Chejop seems like he's one of those dudes who is totally at peace with himself and what he's done and simply passes into Lethe.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:49:43-07:00","id":852663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852658#post852658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Realistically, Chejop seems like he's one of those dudes who is totally at peace with himself and what he's done and simply passes into Lethe.</div> </div> </div> </div>A man who sobs about the fate of Creation after he dies isn't going peacefully into Lethe. Now, he probably really wants to go into Lethe, but the conviction that drove him to do horrible things for the &quot;good of Creation&quot; is going to work against him in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:50:05-07:00","id":852664,"title":"","content":"I think the important thing here is you can do villainous things, even be a villain, but not be a bad or evil person. I mean, the Wyld Hunt kills Solars and Lunars who are innocent of the crime they're accused of (being really demonic monster in a human body), but does that make them evil? Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> The fact you can be a heroic person who intends to do the right thing and BELIEVES you're doing the right thing, even as you are committing some wicked wrong act has nuance and depth. The thing to remember in the OP's idea is... they could be wrong. This might not be helping ANYTHING. They might be true believers trying to make the world a better place and doing something they think only SEEMS horrible to those who don't understand it.<br /> <br /> To quote a character who betrayed humanity and companions for peace with monsters in a story, &quot;Will it be hard? Will there be pains as things change? Of course. But I've determined only a few hundred thousand need die for this! Isn't this worth their sacrifice?&quot; (I probably screwed up the wording, but the idea is there)<br /> <br /> That character believed WITHOUT A DOUBT they were doing the right thing, and it didn't make it any less horrible.<br /> <br /> Edit: It occurs to me, that can be a form of heroism... being a villain and doing something horrible, because you believe it NEEDS to be done. You'll probably be punished and suffer for it after the fact... and yes, you ARE a villain in doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 03-24-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:16:41-07:00","id":852688,"title":"","content":"I for one think it would be great if both the abyssals and deathlords as a whole were morally ambiguous. The fact that we can, with this story idea, have a balanced discussion about whether the abyssals are justified in their actions is VERY encouraging to me!<br /> <br /> &quot;The greater good&quot; is not an ironclad defense of virtue. That's a cornerstone of Exalted writing. It is, however, an excellent device for justifying morally complex characters, which are infinitely superior to flat, morally bankrupt antagonists.<br /> <br /> As to the deathlords, I had not heard this idea that they might have stolen their powers in 3e but that does offer some good story options. Perhaps the neverborn can't control them directly anymore, but Whispers are still very much a thing and none of them walked away unchanged? A few might have the mental fortitude to preserve the core of their morality but I imagine most would be pretty cracked after swallowing a shard of pure screeching madness. Maybe one crafted the great contagion to be a permanent solution to the Underworld's ghost quota, but their madness caused them to carry a decimal point the wrong way, or another deathlord got ahold of the formula and decided to &quot;help&quot; by adding a secret ingredient that made it 100 times more deadly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-25-2016, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:53:36-07:00","id":852703,"title":"","content":"I like the basic idea. What I'd handle it as is more...this is the easy way. Sacrificing ghosts by thousands, funneling death into the underworld, stabilizing the underworld, it's one way to calm the Neverborn. Shut them up, keep Oblivion from growing, etc. But it's the easy way. It's the way they think they can do forever. If they were brave enough to venture into the Labyrinth and do something about it, at great personal cost, then oblivion could be sealed forever. But they don't want to. They don't want to make the personal sacrifice, or may not even know the personal sacrifice option exists. So the Abyssals and their chivalry of death is the route of pushing the sacrifice required to keep things stable onto others. &quot;For the Greater Good&quot;, when in reality, it's for your own good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:09:23-07:00","id":852708,"title":"","content":"Here's an interesting exercise: how much time does each ghost have to be &quot;worth&quot; in order to justify mass murder in Creation? If you knew that every fresh soul would extend the Underworld AND Creation's lifespan by a century, would you do it?<br /> <br /> What if it was just a decade? A year? A season? A month? A week? A day?<br /> <br /> Where do you draw the line? When does it stop being worth it?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Other considerations: since the final goal is a bigger underworld population, you are not <b>just </b>killing people, but &quot;re-purposing&quot; them. Maybe your character has a set of rules for which souls they will or will not take. Maybe they sleep better at night if they only kill the really bad eggs, or maybe they only want the best of the best in their little corner of the afterlife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-25-2016, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:22:17-07:00","id":852716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852567#post852567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esoteric metaphysical justification for concretely bad behavior always strikes me as weaksauce bullshit whenever fantasy fiction authors invoke it for why their bad boys aren't <i>actually</i> bad after all and so the audience doesn't have to feel guilty for liking them. And that's what this sort of thing always amounts to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I don't get the motivation for liking or playing loyalist Abyssals in this case, or even why they're playable at all (beyond my cynical notion of &quot;another book to sell,&quot; and &quot;visual ties to Vampire, which may let us sell more Vampire,&quot; at least with sole regard to past eds of course). It seemed to me that Redemption exists solely for this reason - to justify having a bad person do bad things and then, at least metaphysically, be cleansed from their inherent taint if not the ramifications of their deeds<br /> <br /> I mean, most of the time when you hear discussion of Abyssals, they're either NPC antagonists or PC rebels who are typically seeking redemption (because why not). So there's very little motivation to like them for being bad, because they have an explicit escape clause to badness (Redemption) written right in. Similar to 2e GSPs, except the escape clause was implicit in how the Yozis can't actually make them obey, just try to bribe them indefinitely with HellCoke and demon strippers. But even there, you're somewhat expected to gloss over bad behavior &quot;because what would you do if you were a failure who then got the power cosmic?&quot;<br /> <br /> For that matter, I can't think of one game line that has ever done a pure bad-guy antagonist playable splat well, or facilitated cohesive/coherent &quot;evil PC&quot; games. Plenty have tried, sure.<br /> <br /> Meh, I'm not even sure this is a relevant response!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 03-24-2016, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T21:56:25-07:00","id":852797,"title":"","content":"Will the Exalted fanbase explode if they use the word evil or something ? There are an awful lot of dancing and word-lawyering happening to justifying murder here, you may as well throw in the &quot;They are crazy, so it's okay&quot; cliche so it can meet its brother, &quot;For the Greater Good, so it's okay&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 03-25-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:04:36-07:00","id":852801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852797#post852797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Exalted's fanbase explode if they use the word evil or something ? There is an awful lot of dancing and word-lawyering happening to justifying murder here, you may as well throw in the &quot;They are crazy, so it's okay&quot; cliche so can meet its brother, &quot;For the Greater Good, so it's okay&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/DBsArentNice\" target=\"_blank\">It's generally deliberately avoided, yes.</a> Not because there's no such thing, but because good/evil judgments, once invoked, tend to dominate the discussion, but are not as relevant to how most people <i>actually go about living their lives</i> as a somewhat less judgmental examination of peoples' internal motivations and how they relate to others personally.<br /> <br /> There's probably a comparison to be made with how once you start explaining the setting in terms of Primordials and the First Age, it tends to dominate the material and you lose focus on the setting as it exists in the present.<br /> <br /> (I'm actually much less inclined to give Sesus Nagezzer a pass on his pimping than Geoff was, I think.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 03-25-2016, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:07:04-07:00","id":852803,"title":"","content":"I think in the end it's just spitballing to think of reasons as to why anyone in their right mind would play an Abyssal in a mixed circle without feeling like the guy who brought an Antipaladin to the &quot;Let's save the princess and rescue the kingdom&quot; DnD adventure. Or even play an Abyssal in an all-Abyssal group and not feel like just another cackling puppy-muncher or dreary nihilist. If the Devs deliver on their promises to expand the roles of the Deathknights and give the fanbase more options, threads like this will probably vanish real quick.<br /> <br /> Edit: Because going by 2E, you can't really avoid the words Evil when talking about Abyssals, because 2E Loyalist Abyssals were the closest things to genuine , unadulterated, no ifs ands buts or moral relativism EVIL this side of the bad interpretation of the Ebon Dragon. Ninety percent of all plotting my Abyssal-loving friends did for their character concepts was how to be an Abyssal who wasn't a kitten-choking infant-stomping village-burning villain without everything exploding around them forever and without just having a very roundabout character generation for a new Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","user":"Grindavikur","date":". 03-25-2016, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:24:38-07:00","id":852809,"title":"","content":"2e overdid it, to understate things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:18:32-07:00","id":852834,"title":"","content":"I think without Resonance to force you to be evil, it's not such an issue.<br /> <br /> But still;<br /> <br /> The thing with Abyssals is that they had a goal. And either you followed the goal (destroy the world) or you rebelled against it (and thus were defined by your rebellion).<br /> <br /> Lunars also had a goal, but could take it or leave it, and had various sub-goals within that goal.<br /> (And I notice that with 3rd ed, it seems like only about half of them care about this goal)<br /> <br /> Sidereals had a job. About half of them also had a goal, and then maybe another 20% had a different goal, and the remainder didn't care about either.<br /> <br /> Solars didn't have a goal, they had a wide variety of goals.<br /> <br /> Abyssals were more defined by the goal (of destroying the world) than anyone else was, and that was restrictive.<br /> You couldn't play a wandering vampire hero with death-themed powers without thinking about this goal (how did you escape your Deathlord? If you didn't want to destroy the world, why did you become an Abyssal?) the way you could play a wandering bestial hero with shapechanging powers without thinking about their goal (maybe you've never encountered the Realm), which made it much harder to join the group of wandering human heroes with superhuman powers.<br /> <br /> I really like Abyssals in terms of their themes, but the goal makes them very restrictive as both antagonists and protagonists.<br /> <br /> It sounds like 3rd ed is going to have a much wider variety of goals for the Deathlords, which translates into a wider variety of goals for Abyssals, but hopefully it will also allow a much wider variety of individualised goals for Abyssals.<br /> <br /> They're 100 mighty, dark and blasphemous antiheroes, I'd like them to be able to have a wide variety of goals, good*, bad, alien, amoral and individual, just like the 150 mighty heroes of the Sun have a wide variety of goals.<br /> *In an anti-heroic way.<br /> <br /> So. I don't have a problem with there being some Abyssals that believe that killing people placates Oblivion and thus saves the world. But I wouldn't want it to be the goal of 100 Abyssals. Same as I wouldn't 100 Abyssals to want to kill people in order to destroy the world. I want 10 of each, 20 who are just out for conquest, 30 who are loyal to the Deathlords and their variety of goals, and another 30 with a wide range of individual goals.<br /> <br /> You need some Abyssals who do want to murder the world for when you want straight villains with no moral greyness.<br /> You need some Abyssals who want to murder the world for a reason that is, to them, heroic, so you can have straight villains with more versimillitude.<br /> But you don't need all Abyssals to be like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-25-2016, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:27:58-07:00","id":852837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852797#post852797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Exalted's fanbase explode if they use the word evil or something ? There is an awful lot of dancing and word-lawyering happening to justifying murder here, you may as well throw in the &quot;They are crazy, so it's okay&quot; cliche so can meet its brother, &quot;For the Greater Good, so it's okay&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not like mass-murder stops being evil just because your character had a good reason for it. Making Abyssals less evil is not really the point. The aim is to make them something more complex that I would maybe want to play and write stories for.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And as Wizard said, writing an entire splat into a single narrative corner (or one corner and the corner opposite it) is not fun for the player or storyteller. The measure of a setting's success is in how many directions the presented material allows you to go. 2e Abyssals fail this test rather hard, as a mission statement of &quot;<i><b>MURDER EVERYTHING</b></i>&quot; does not leave much room for exploring concepts beyond that of a psychotic killer. If the broader goal of Abyssals was &quot;save the Underworld and Creation by keeping Oblivion in check&quot; then this could be the traditional path to doing that but many players might explore other concepts with the same result, in addition to following the established path or abandoning their mission statement entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-25-2016, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T03:16:34-07:00","id":852872,"title":"","content":"quick question actually now that we are talking about grey zone deathlords, did the Bodhisattva actually do anything like straight up evil? I mean he made a pretty functioning society the only big difference from other places i can think of is that when your grandma dies she doesn't disappear, she's just transparent now. She still bakes awesome cookies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T05:11:43-07:00","id":852901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852633#post852633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for describing exactly why I dislike Madoka Magica.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> I've never been clear if the writer didn't fully understand the concept of entropy or if we're supposed to take the fact that Kyubey cares so little for Earth's survival provided a quota of energy is met as a sign that this isn't really about prolonging the life of the universe. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T05:46:20-07:00","id":852909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852872#post852872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">quick question actually now that we are talking about grey zone deathlords, did the Bodhisattva actually do anything like straight up evil? I mean he made a pretty functioning society the only big difference from other places i can think of is that when your grandma dies she doesn't disappear, she's just transparent now. She still bakes awesome cookies.</div> </div> </div> </div>He soulforges tons of ghosts and claims they've gone to paradise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:44:17-07:00","id":852935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852797#post852797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the Exalted fanbase explode if they use the word evil or something ? There are an awful lot of dancing and word-lawyering happening to justifying murder here, you may as well throw in the &quot;They are crazy, so it's okay&quot; cliche so it can meet its brother, &quot;For the Greater Good, so it's okay&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a general Western thing, or my local corner of if, or just something that's more particular to my circle of friends and family, and the way we talk, but &quot;evil&quot; is kind of reserved for an elemental, supernatural force, the kind of malevolent thing that's chases down Ash Williams or flows from Sauron or what have you. Which is something I don't I really believe in, but a lot of older Western culture, and religious Western culture, particularly, does.<br /> <br /> (Like, as an example, I was watching the old Shaolin Temple movie with the brother last week, and it was unintentionally hilarious to us where in the dub whenever the crusty old abbot at Shaolin Temple kept on describing Jet Li's character, a young man with some violent impulses and anger, with &quot;he looks evil&quot;. Rather than &quot;bad&quot;, or &quot;violent&quot;, or &quot;dangerous&quot;, or &quot;nasty&quot;, or &quot;criminal&quot;, or &quot;cruel&quot;, or &quot;selfish&quot;. It's, like... really, this kid? &quot;Evil&quot;? Isn't that just a *little* hyperbolic, Mr Witchfinder General?)<br /> <br /> People who are a bit more loose lipped around the word &quot;evil&quot; applying it to stuff I would just say is bad or criminal, might not have the same reaction. This is kind of the vibe of why I feel like evil doesn't crop up in Exalted, as well as what Stephen says, because there just plainly isn't that kind of force about, and it just feels wrong to use the word.<br /> <br /> (Even the Wyld or Oblivion, the closest there is to evil, is like, well, the destruction of Creation is a means to an ends (reaching a kind of spiritual peace, of sorts), for these, getting rid of something in the way of what they *actually* want, not anything that is what I'd think of as supernatural evil, where the suffering and destruction is the point. And why the introduction of the 2e Infernals version of the Ebon Dragon didn't work well.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T06:44:26-07:00","id":852936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852834#post852834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like 3rd ed is going to have a much wider variety of goals for the Deathlords, which translates into a wider variety of goals for Abyssals, but hopefully it will also allow a much wider variety of individualised goals for Abyssals.<br /> <br /> They're 100 mighty, dark and blasphemous antiheroes, I'd like them to be able to have a wide variety of goals, good*, bad, alien, amoral and individual, just like the 150 mighty heroes of the Sun have a wide variety of goals.<br /> *In an anti-heroic way.</div> </div> </div> </div>My ideal state is one where being a loyalist is mostly doing the Things You Want<sup>1</sup> with the blessing and support of a Deathlord, in return for occasionally doing the Thing <i>They</i> Want. Now, the latter will, from time to time, be atrocities, but they'll mostly be the kind of atrocities that align with your interests or are easy to justify to yourself.<br /> <br /> Renegades, then, should be the Abyssals who <i>can't</i> justify those things to themselves, or who ultimately can't deal with the dark power inside them.<br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>This includes unabashedly &quot;good&quot; things, like freeing slaves and fighting for the downtrodden and what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:12:17-07:00","id":852949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852909#post852909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He soulforges tons of ghosts and claims they've gone to paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>An invention of 2e.<br /> <br /> Mind you, making a society that glorifies death and sets the dead over the living is still not really all that nice, even if the existence of ghosts is proven. After all, and I'm sure the restless dead would agree with me on this, being dead may have its perks, but it's not the same as being alive - you lose quite a few things, and in time forget you even had them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:20:09-07:00","id":852955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852909#post852909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He soulforges tons of ghosts and claims they've gone to paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmmm i wonder what type of ghosts it is though, like are they all ghosts of big bad criminals or &quot;dissidents&quot; so to speak... though i doubt he would say that the criminals goes to paradise","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:27:50-07:00","id":852961,"title":"","content":"No, just regular ghosts that aren't that useful.<br /> <br /> I forget what he did in 1e though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:33:34-07:00","id":852964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852961#post852961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget what he did in 1e though.</div> </div> </div> </div>He set himself up as this bodhisattva figure and ruled over Skullstone, and acted as patron to a number of Abyssals. Did he <i>need</i> to do something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:36:53-07:00","id":852965,"title":"","content":"Not really. I didn't say he did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T07:46:32-07:00","id":852970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">exactly why I dislike Madoka Magica</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Madoka Magica is all about how all of its exploitation and cruelty in the name of preserving the universe isn't the least bit justified. When a particular character is trying to openly argue with the protagonist that she should sacrifice herself for the good of the universe, wholly oblivious to her fears and objections, it's all framed in terms of that character really <i>not getting it</i>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-25-2016, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:16:30-07:00","id":852976,"title":"","content":"Another reason I find the premise of &quot;Abyssals are actually good because killing people keeps the black hole in the middle of the Underworld from eating everything&quot; to because I find it to lack about as much credibility as the idea that mortals can't found lasting nations without a Lunar over their shoulder, re. the Underworld has had plenty of ghosts since long before there were ever Abyssals.<br /> <br /> That and how there's nothing really specific to the Abyssals to enable such a goal. Hell, if killing people and making sure they left ghosts was necessary, the Realm and the Guild would probably be vastly better equipped to do it. Double the human tribute and have the surplus ritualistically killed; there's the Realm 'saving Creation' again.<br /> <br /> The idea that complex social rituals and elaborate financial transactions hold of the chaos of the Wyld and reinforce the shape of expanded Creation is, I presume, not really about the Wyld, it's an existential metaphor for the significance of things like codification and economics on our lives and our experience of the world.<br /> <br /> What is needing to repeatedly murder people an existential metaphor for? The dependence of modern economics, especially as experienced in the most affluent countries, on exploitative systems that undeniably lead to the suffering and death of uncomfortably large numbers of invisible people? Maybe you could do it like that, but I feel that the metaphor would become so overbooked with fantasy wank as to be obscured, and that the setting already contains things that relate such issues better, in the form of the Realm and the Guild.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I quite like how Masters of Jade made that whole thing of &quot;the Guild propitiates Fair Folk by feeding them people&quot; thing more than just &quot;maybe the Guild is ugly but justified&quot; by creating plot hooks and backstory out of how such a system of exploitation is not sustainable in the long run. Kind of the classic &quot;the king tries to save the kingdom by feeding the dragon peasants, but then runs out of peasants&quot; thing. But I digress.<br /> <br /> I have my own ideas for how one can portray and play Abyssals who don't go for obvious rebel narratives without making them cackling supervillains, but that's probably for another time. For now, I'll just maintain that I find any attempt to make them useful cosmic arbiters to mostly be trite.<br /> <br /> There are certain mildly similar things I would find to be a bit more functional, though, and relate to my ideas for them; things akin to working in a system like Aztec human sacrifice, shaping societies towards a reflection on the mortality of the universe, made stark in this apparent last age of Creation.<br /> <br /> Part of what makes them work more to me is that they necessarily involve the greater social context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:33:09-07:00","id":852985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852803#post852803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the end it's just spitballing to think of reasons as to why anyone in their right mind would play an Abyssal in a mixed circle without feeling like the guy who brought an Antipaladin to the &quot;Let's save the princess and rescue the kingdom&quot; DnD adventure. Or even play an Abyssal in an all-Abyssal group and not feel like just another cackling puppy-muncher or dreary nihilist. If the Devs deliver on their promises to expand the roles of the Deathknights and give the fanbase more options, threads like this will probably vanish real quick.<br /> <br /> Edit: Because going by 2E, you can't really avoid the words Evil when talking about Abyssals, because 2E Loyalist Abyssals were the closest things to genuine , unadulterated, no ifs ands buts or moral relativism EVIL this side of the bad interpretation of the Ebon Dragon. Ninety percent of all plotting my Abyssal-loving friends did for their character concepts was how to be an Abyssal who wasn't a kitten-choking infant-stomping village-burning villain without everything exploding around them forever and without just having a very roundabout character generation for a new Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly certain you could say the same about 1e Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:15:59-07:00","id":853005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852803#post852803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ninety percent of all plotting my Abyssal-loving friends did for their character concepts was how to be an Abyssal who wasn't a kitten-choking infant-stomping village-burning villain without everything exploding around them forever and without just having a very roundabout character generation for a new Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to be a jerk here, but it sounds like your friends didn't <i>actually</i> love Abyssals. They loved the idea of Abyssals they had in their heads that was utterly unsupported by the actual Abyssals the setting gave you.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with that per se, but... why bash your head against that wall?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:48:58-07:00","id":853032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853005#post853005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not trying to be a jerk here, but it sounds like your friends didn't <i>actually</i> love Abyssals. They loved the idea of Abyssals they had in their heads that was utterly unsupported by the actual Abyssals the setting gave you.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with that per se, but... why bash your head against that wall?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the argument could be made that 2E Abyssals were a boring binary choice of character options and that people can be in love with the idea of Deaths Chosen, but not the execution. Resonance was a very clumsy, hamfisted way trying to make Abyssals have a reason to be villainous, and that there are better, more interesting options for giving Abyssals reasons to be a loyalist and reasons to be a rebel, and more grey area in between. All stick no carrot does not a fun mechanic make. Even Limit Break gives you a hefty reward in completely refilling your willpower. Resonance was ABSURDLY strict. Being friendly with a mortal, not even saving their lives or anything, but just sitting down for a cup of tea and having a conversation where you had no ulterior motive? Resonance. Living anything like a mortal unless your boss specifically told you to do so for reasons? Have fun exploding/losing the use of a limb/getting possessed. Or eating lethal damage to try and make your boss happy. Or doing a big bunch of sacrifices to get them off your ass. Resonance was so incredibly limiting that any character concept that didn't treat every mortal you met as a tool, zombie fodder, sacrifice material, or blithering idiot to be ignored was going to have a very fun time exploding. A lot. <br /> <br /> I could say that the &quot;loving the idea of a splat in their heads unsupported by actual book&quot; argument could also be made for anyone who likes DB as anything but incredibly weak mooks who can't even use their perfect-defense when someone modifies their attack with a charm, constantly manipulated by everything around them, who are objectively pathetic usurpers who should just roll over and let their Solar masters return to the fore. Or someone who likes Lunars as anything but cowards hiding at the edge of creation doing nothing but sitting with their thumbs up their butts for a few millenia. Or people who want to play Alchemicals as anything but really, really needing to just call in the Solars to fix everything already. Or anyone who likes Infernals as...<br /> <br /> Well, we all know how many people like to just ignore the first few chapters of the Infernals book. Point is, Exalted already has a long history of people saying that the current take on a splat is wrong and it could be fixed by doing (xyz). And this edition, there's seemingly a lot of talk from the devs as well saying that, in 2E, mistakes were made about splat-writing. <br /> <br /> But! The argument could also be made that you don't need to worry about making Abyssals a playable splat, and that it's okay for there to be an Exalt type that's the unabashed villains of the setting. But, personally, I think having a pure villain exalt type smacks up against how Exalted likes to talk a big game about classical heroism v. modern heroism, moral relativism, might makes right, etc. Being a Creature of Darkness is the closest thing to being declared objectively evil in the setting, and any Solar with the right charm can declare Jeff a CoD for telling a lame joke or cutting them off in traffic. <br /> <br /> I fully expect the Chivalry of Death to be as in-depth a mechanic as Resonance was; I'm a-okay with Abyssals having the most complex limit-break replacement in the game. I'm totally fine with them being weighed down with the most chains of loyalty, obligation, servitude, etc. But I'd hope and I think those friends of mine might hope it's more interesting and shades-of-grey this time around. I'm a-okay with all of Abyssals moral tones being far closer to black than white. But I'm really hoping we get a few more shades instead of complete dickishness or &quot;I really wanna be a Solar already&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:06:26-07:00","id":853099,"title":"","content":"The problem with Oblivion is that it tries to reshift the focus of the entire game. It sends the message that the battles over the Realm and the like don't really matter compared to this inevitable world-destroying force at the root of the world that must be confronted. Making the Deathlords and Abyssals into its enemies rather than its soldiers helps them a bit, but doesn't address the underlying problem.<br /> <br /> I expect that 3e will remove Oblivion (at least as it was before) entirely. The problem with it wasn't just that it made Abyssals too dark and evil; the problem was that it shifted their focus away from the mortal affairs of Creation and tried to pull everything else along with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853005#post853005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to be a jerk here, but it sounds like your friends didn't <i>actually</i> love Abyssals. They loved the idea of Abyssals they had in their heads that was utterly unsupported by the actual Abyssals the setting gave you.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with that per se, but... why bash your head against that wall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we zoom out and look at the bigger picture... the problem is that <i>most</i> people didn't love Abyssals. It had few fans. And the fans it did have often caused the problem I mentioned above with Oblivion. Abyssals actually had all the problems 2e Infernals did regarding disrupting the tone and focus of the game.<br /> <br /> I've mentioned this with regards to Infernals, but it affected Abyssals, too... I think that if you look at, say, your typical Final Fantasy game, there's a moment when the game is done introducing you to the world and says &quot;all right, now you're going to fight a superdemon.&quot; And from then on the story is all about killing a monster clown or an evil tree or a Sephiroth or whatever, and the other stuff stops mattering so much. And I think that because that kind of storytelling has become so widespread in videogames, people expect it out of Exalted. But I also think it's really really bad for a tabletop game, since it means you're discarding most of what matters to the main game.<br /> <br /> So this whole &quot;Oblivion as the cosmic enemy of the entire universe&quot; or &quot;The Ebon Dragon as Big Bad of the entire setting&quot; is a bad thing, not just because it takes away from the rest of the game, but because it's so much the default in many fantasy stories nowadays that players (and, yes, writers) will gravitate to it if you're not careful. And when you start having it seeping into canon, it's also a bit like... that problem you run into where you make an NPC more interesting than the PCs, sort of? You're taking one specific story and letting it take over the setting, which makes the whole setting more one-dimensional and harder to use to tell anything else.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest complaints people had about Abyssals was that they were really only good for telling two stories. (And I'd take that a step further -- they were really only good for telling one story, you just got to choose which side you were on in it.) I think it's reasonable for players to look in askance at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 01-26-2020, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T12:53:10-07:00","id":853129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852566#post852566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool idea up til this point. The Empress's action hero bit shouldn't be retconned to &quot;because a Solar let her.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I completely agree. It just seemed like another thing that would humanize the Deathlords further. And it also wrecks one of the coolest characters in the setting, the bit that proves that Dragon Blooded matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852601#post852601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The greater good.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I was really hoping I wouldn't be left hanging there. lol<br /> <br /> <br /> I would also like to say that &quot;the greater good&quot; I mentioned is pretty objectively awful. Like I said, black on gray morality is pretty unappealing. It's terrible for the Exalted universe, which has no objective lesson or horrible conclusion. It'd be terrible for any game that isn't like Call of Cthulhu really.<br /> <br /> Works great in the SCP universe where you're told that they have the will to save humanity when anyone else would allow humanity to die, because they're willing to rape an innocent woman so she won't give birth to the apocalypse. They're the good guys who will do whatever it takes to save the world, even burn half of it to the ground to save the other half. Are you really good after that? I can't really answer that, but it does math out to being the better option.<br /> Disclaimer: Rape is bad, m'kay. Story I reference here: <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231</a><br /> <br /> Again, would not use this twist for Exalted. Ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 03-25-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:09:42-07:00","id":853157,"title":"","content":"hmmmmmm what if instead of destroying creation and shoving it all down the world ending drain known as oblivion, the neverborn wanted to &quot;merge&quot; creation and the underworld in an attempt to &quot;remove&quot; death and give them back their lives so to speak, this way the neverborn wont be ordering the deathlords to destroy everything, the deathlords won't order the abyssals to destroy or do other stuff like that and the abyssals will probably still do their own thing but eh....<br /> <br /> anyhow that's just something i thought of there, it also it lets the deathlords and in a way the abyssals do whatever they want since not even the neverborn knows how to merge the worlds or if it actually works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:19:54-07:00","id":853161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along#post851941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is just a story idea I'd like to workshop, not in any way a suggestion for the next edition of Abyssal Exalted or Exalted canon in general,<br /> <br /> But what if most Deathknights were actively working to <i>subvert</i> Oblivion by ensuring a steady stream of souls into the Underworld? In 2nd ed Stygia was a First Age project to bind Oblivion and ensure that it never swallowed Creation whole by using ghosts as stabilizing elements. Taking that an extra step, I have this notion that Deathknights might spread death and misery in Creation in order to ensure that enough ghosts enter the afterlife to keep the Maw from spreading.<br /> <br /> This would most likely be little understood by the living people they terrorize, and it's not to their benefit to be forthcoming with their reasoning. The end result would be Deathknights that on the surface seem like heartless abominations prowling Creation for hapless victims, but who's actions can be at least partially justified by the fact that if they <i>don't </i>do this, Oblivion may grow and bring final death to all things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait... So this whole time, the Deathknights have just been the most Tsundere exalt in the game?!<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not destroying this village because I *LIKE* creation or anything... Baka!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1401,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","user":"rungok","date":". 03-25-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:30:55-07:00","id":853164,"title":"","content":"There are some themes that are appropriate to Abyssal stories that arent appropriate to any other splat. This is also true for Lunars, Sidereals, Dragon Bloods and Infernals. That is thematic distinction at work, and it's a good thing! It means those splats feel unique, and it means you can approach the setting from angles you could not before. And I think part and parcel of the Abyssal experience is death and loss. Not pointless futility necessarily, which was what we were forced to swallow in 2e, but a profound sense that life is finite, that the here and now matters, and that you can lose everything if you make the wrong choices. Another theme of great importance is that life is consumption. When one man lives another dies for him, we all live on borrowed time and we take big loans out on each others' credit.<br /> <br /> For the Abyssals and their stories to feel unique and to offer this narrative (which is the main reason I find them interesting) I bellieve that Oblivion is a necessary setting element. Because without Oblivion, nothing in Exalted actually ends. It just gets recycled, or repurposed. And that narrative works great for Lunars and Solars, but personally I prefer a story where death really matters and overshadows the players' actions. When I want to tell a story with those themes I write an Abyssal story, because that splat gives me those options.<br /> <br /> That said, Oblivion might be changing in 3e for the better. There was no mention of the Maw in the backer pdf, and it seems that the labrynth may be getting a metaphysical rewrite as well. Oblivion might not be seen by anyone, but the Deathlords know its there, or fear it enough to take these sorts of precautions. Maybe it's only accessible by the labrynth, and the mad ghosts that return upon seeing it give conflicting reports on its size and threat. The Abyssals would by no means be the first to fight this unknown force, but they are the greatest champions on the field at present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-25-2016, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:12:21-07:00","id":853183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect that 3e will remove Oblivion (at least as it was before) entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see good prospects in the corebook that oblivion will now be what happens to people who get lost in the rivers, wells and encircling sea of the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:45:53-07:00","id":853201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853164#post853164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not pointless futility necessarily, which was what we were forced to swallow in 2e, but a profound sense that life is finite, that the here and now matters, and that you can lose everything if you make the wrong choices. Another theme of great importance is that life is consumption. When one man lives another dies for him, we all live on borrowed time and we take big loans out on each others' credit.<br /> <br /> For the Abyssals and their stories to feel unique and to offer this narrative (which is the main reason I find them interesting) I bellieve that Oblivion is a necessary setting element. Because without Oblivion, nothing in Exalted actually ends. It just gets recycled, or repurposed. And that narrative works great for Lunars and Solars, but personally I prefer a story where death really matters and overshadows the players' actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does death not matter? When a person dies, their soul may linger for a while, even a long while, but will pretty much inevitably pass on barring becoming a nephwrack. Once you go through Lethe, that person-who-was is irrevocably gone. They no longer exist. The soul is fundamentally destroyed for all purposes that really matter, like identity and experience. The fact that the soul itself is recycled, if it even is, doesn't matter, because whoever is born with that soul cannot be the last person who had it. Lethe recycling isn't some happy event where the prior life-experience somehow stays conscious and communes with UCS and the shinma for eternity or something. It's gone, period.<br /> <br /> Death is an ending even without a big malicious hole at the bottom dating to prehistory that is &quot;real death&quot; versus some notion that Lethe, aka the in-setting permanent cessation of a life-experience, is somehow &quot;fake death,&quot; or even that people who die and linger as ghosts aren't lessened irrevocably in the process. Death matters for all Exalted. When they kill someone, they can't just take it back, ever. An Exalt that dies loses their Exalted status and is in no way guaranteed to carry on - the vast majority don't. Not near everyone lingers as a ghost, and it's not an experience anyone should really rationally desire - wanting to do so should be inherently <i>irrational </i>and tied in some way to the fear of non-existence that, as far as we know IRL, is death, and what in-setting would be Lethe, <i>not that many people in-setting really know the details of how that works either</i>. Death is still scary when you can linger on in the Underworld - you're you in some ways but narrower in others, and I think every ghost knows that they won't persist forever, and then what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T16:10:49-07:00","id":853215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853201#post853201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does death not matter? When a person dies, their soul may linger for a while, even a long while, but will pretty much inevitably pass on barring becoming a nephwrack. Once you go through Lethe, that person-who-was is irrevocably gone. They no longer exist. The soul is fundamentally destroyed for all purposes that really matter, like identity and experience. The fact that the soul itself is recycled, if it even is, doesn't matter, because whoever is born with that soul cannot be the last person who had it. Lethe recycling isn't some happy event where the prior life-experience somehow stays conscious and communes with UCS and the shinma for eternity or something. It's gone, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much a philosophical difference that doesnt bear into practical play in most games, but I see a big difference between being wiped clean and being erased. I generally see the soul as the true self, the point of perspective that defines us as separate from others, and having that snuffed out is a big deal. From an external perspective its not much different; grandma isnt going to bake you her special peanut butter cookies again either way. But it makes a big difference to grandma whether shes losing her memories or losing everything she ever will be and ever was.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is existentially terrifying in a way reincarnation is not. It adds a different flavor to the story, one that I enjoy for the dark gothic narrative endemic to the Abyssal exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T16:24:38-07:00","id":853221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853215#post853215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is very much a philosophical difference that doesnt bear into practical play in most games, but I see a big difference between being wiped clean and being erased. I generally see the soul as the true self, the point of perspective that defines us as separate from others, and having that snuffed out is a big deal. From an external perspective its not much different; grandma isnt going to bake you her special peanut butter cookies again either way. But it makes a big difference to grandma whether shes losing her memories or losing everything she ever will be and ever was.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is existentially terrifying in a way reincarnation is not. It adds a different flavor to the story, one that I enjoy for the dark gothic narrative endemic to the Abyssal exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reincarnation is equally terrifying. Eastern religion has this weird idea we don't much talk about where there really is no memory, personality, or true self inherent in the soul. The soul is kinda just a bundle of karmic debt and there's no real continuity when you reincarnate.<br /> <br /> To me, there is little practical difference between having your soul destroyed and being reincarnated. You're not coming back different, the you that once existed is pretty much just gone forever. <br /> <br /> Might as well just say there is no heaven, no individual continuity, that your soul has been destroyed forever. Basically the same from a western cultural perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T16:41:35-07:00","id":853227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853221#post853221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reincarnation is equally terrifying. Eastern religion has this weird idea we don't much talk about where there really is no memory, personality, or true self inherent in the soul. The soul is kinda just a bundle of karmic debt and there's no real continuity when you reincarnate.<br /> <br /> To me, there is little practical difference between having your soul destroyed and being reincarnated. You're not coming back different, the you that once existed is pretty much just gone forever.<br /> <br /> Might as well just say there is no heaven, no individual continuity, that your soul has been destroyed forever. Basically the same from a western cultural perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is interesting. And legit horrifying. Why is this the first I've heard of this? My impression was VERY different in Exalted, especially with things like the Past Lives merit. If this was how reincarnation worked in Exalted then you could play this up for Abyssals and then maybe you wouldn't need the narrative device of Oblivion, but is that actually how it works in Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-26-2016, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T17:36:40-07:00","id":853243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853227#post853227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is interesting. And legit horrifying. Why is this the first ive heard of this? My impression was VERY different in Exalted, especially with things like the Past Lives merit. If this was how reincarnation worked in Exaltrd then you could play this up for Abyssals and then maybe you wouldnt need the narrative device of Oblivion, but is that actually how it works in Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With the five seconds of research I've done since college on the subject, it seems there is divide over what reincarnation precisely is. OF COURSE the entirety of eastern religion would have different conceptions of the soul and the afterlife, just as we do in the west. I feel kind of stupid assuming it was fairly homogenous.<br /> <br /> SO, Buddhism takes a pretty dim view of the soul. Anything defining the self, such as memories and personality, are wiped clean. Which you'd want, because the self is just a barrier to escaping reincarnation (actually called redeath, because dying really sucks). So just what I was saying. BUT, plenty of others apparently view it the way you expected, with a quick perusal of Hinduism's Jiva (soul) being made up of sense, mind, intellect, and ego. This ALONG WITH the Atman, or higher soul, reincarnates too.<br /> <br /> So I guess it really depends on who you ask? Think western questions like &quot;Who gets into heaven?&quot; and &quot;Is heaven really a place with clouds and halos and wings and pearly gates, or will it be completely unrecognizable?&quot; Each sect answers these questions differently.<br /> <br /> Note: This is all really shallow research. I'd have to bust out old textbooks and do hours of research, and I'm a little busy with work for that these days. Ah, adult responsibilities.<br /> <br /> As for how Exalted answers things, I think the answer is &quot;Shrug&quot;. Not much word count has been spilled on word-of-god statements on the nature of the soul, I think.<br /> <br /> Do mortals have past lives or is that just Exaltations?<br /> <br /> Also note that Exalted has no tradition of escaping the wheel of reincarnation, so from a religious standpoint it's bleak as hell. The best you can hope for is becoming an Exalt for a few hundred or thousand years. But you'll still be wiped clean by reincarnation eventually regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 03-25-2016, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T18:18:16-07:00","id":853263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853243#post853243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also note that Exalted has no tradition of escaping the wheel of reincarnation...</div> </div> </div> </div>Becoming a ghost; Skullstone even has a religion about it. It's not necessarily a permanent escape, considering that they can still get forced into Lethe again, but in theory a ghost could persist forever. Especially if he gets forged into soulsteel. Which is hardly something to look up to.<br /> <br /> Also, souls were destroyed or dissolved in both the Primordial War and the Balorian Crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T20:00:08-07:00","id":853291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853183#post853183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I see good prospects in the corebook that oblivion will now be what happens to people who get lost in the rivers, wells and encircling sea of the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Oblivion as &quot;sometimes people don't reincarnate&quot; is fine.<br /> <br /> Oblivion as an embodied cosmological enemy of the entire universe that will inevitably consume all things, though, was never really a good fit for Exalted. It's hard to tell a story about human-scale heroes when your enemy is the cosmological concept of Entropy across the entire universe. The inevitability of death is better used as an abstract than as an evil, sentient force.<br /> <br /> I think that that's part of what I hated about it, too. Like -- it can be cool to look at Lookshy and philosophize about the inevitability of its fall, or to look at ruins and consider how everything eventually comes to ruin, etc. But when you embody entropy as this sentient evil <i>force</i>, you can't do that anymore, because now the cycle of empires falling into ruin is all the handiwork of a single cosmic enemy whose ultimate victory is assured. It actually makes death itself less interesting by making it axiomatically impossible for anyone to ever come to terms with it in a narratively interesting fashion.<br /> <br /> Like, in a setting with Oblivion, the end of the Epic of Gilgamesh becomes basically &quot;and then Gilgamesh came to terms with his death, and somewhere deep in the underworld, Oblivion cackled evilly at another inevitable victory, having crushed Gilgamesh's heroic spirit at last by getting him to realize that Oblivion would always triumph.&quot; That's not what that ending is supposed to mean! And it's a problem that hits Abyssals the hardest, because they're the ones who are supposed to be thinking the most about death, and making Oblivion this sinister semi-sentient cosmic force stripped them of the ability to do that in a classically-heroic manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-26-2016, 05:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T20:15:11-07:00","id":853301,"title":"","content":"As much as I love Oblivion as a narrative device, I will shed exactly zero gothic tears if the Neverborn and the Maw are written out of 3e. The fact that sometimes souls just disappear is a perfectly satisfying narrative device. Maybe no one knows why, maybe very few people even know that it happens at all. A final death which is little understood except that it happens, can target anyone, and possibly that it is happening more frequently over time, is much more scary than a giant hole in the ground that communicates its will through the corpse bodies of dead titans.<br /> <br /> I for one think it would be most effective to say that Oblivion does exist, but not in any physical sense unless you're in the labrynth. Outside of that, Deathlords simply know that sometimes things in the Underworld disappear without warning or passing into Lethe, and that they are losing more and more real estate to it over time. They posit that more ghosts will stabilize the area, which may or may not be objectively true, and the chivalry of death is born of their frantic desire to save themselves. The Abyssals are made as weapons with the greater purpose of combating this unknown force, possibly with charms that immunize them from Oblivion, and are tasked with bringing more ghosts into the fold because that's what their bosses think will save their world. And maybe a few of them want to try a different solution, or maybe it turns out that the Deathlords themselves are what is causing this loss, though they don't realize it. Options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-26-2016, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T20:24:36-07:00","id":853304,"title":"","content":"I always felt like the &quot;Oblivion as malicious, sentient, and going to destroy all.&quot; was better as IN GAME propaganda. Probably not the best... but some deathlord probably thinks it's convincing. I prefer if by default at game start, Oblivion is the biggest question mark. &quot;Well, we sent some explorers in, they never came out. We assume they were destroyed.&quot; &quot;What if it's that there's such an awesome party in there, even light doesn't want to leave?&quot; &quot;That... would be terribly disturbing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T20:51:31-07:00","id":853307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853227#post853227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is interesting. And legit horrifying. Why is this the first ive heard of this? My impression was VERY different in Exalted, especially with things like the Past Lives merit. If this was how reincarnation worked in Exaltrd then you could play this up for Abyssals and then maybe you wouldnt need the narrative device of Oblivion, but is that actually how it works in Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Past lives are basically like if you took random pages of an intangible diary and stuck them onto an Exaltation, remembered from a soul that no longer exists in the form it did when it was Exalted, if it exists at all anymore. <br /> <br /> It's a little weird at least with 3e because Exaltations aren't really presented as tangible Things anymore that can be pruned like bonsais (ugh) but the notion of remembering a past life is certainly retained this ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:33:59-07:00","id":853496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852632#post852632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think weird metaphysical justification for immoral action is a hack writing move, because the writer invents the metaphysics. You can justify a convoluted metaphysical reason for <i>anything</i> being &quot;For the greater good,&quot; up to and including the actual historical Holocaust, and if you're the writer and thus get to decide the objective, from-an-omniscient-point-of-view truth of your metaphysics, who's to gainsay you? But the reader is fully <i>aware</i> that it's all just a bunch of arbitrary bullshit you made up, and that you <i>can</i> construct a set of supernatural universal rules to any specification you desire. I know that whenever I encounter a writer who wants to paint a mass murderer as &quot;Not actually evil&quot; because handwave handwave cosmic balance, I immediately think &quot;This writer wants to incorporate mass murder into his stories but actually engaging with it in any way but the most superficial makes him uncomfortable.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My hope is that 3e Sidereals rejects this line of thought as thoroughly as StephenLS does! The Usurpation (as discussed upthread) is one thing; coldly consequentialist murder of random persons &quot;For the Greater Good&quot; because otherwise Fate will cease turning according to The Plan, though, strikes me as exactly what is being talked about in the above quote...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:54:19-07:00","id":853512,"title":"","content":"Say, if the FA Solar doesn't die then Creation will, 100% without a shadow of doubt, go kaboom, right ? Or is it Sidereal/DB apologist's propaganda ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:59:58-07:00","id":853516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853512#post853512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, if the FA Solar doesn't die then Creation will, 100% without a shadow of doubt, go kaboom, right ? Or is it Sidereal/DB apologist's propaganda ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, the prophecy said that guiding the Solars out of their madness had a chance of success as well - the Bronze Faction basically decided that was a risk they couldn't take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:11:19-07:00","id":853528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My hope is that 3e Sidereals rejects this line of thought as thoroughly as StephenLS does! The Usurpation (as discussed upthread) is one thing; coldly consequentialist murder of random persons &quot;For the Greater Good&quot; because otherwise Fate will cease turning according to The Plan, though, strikes me as exactly what is being talked about in the above quote...</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends.<br /> <br /> If it's &quot;you must murder this baby because otherwise the world will stop working&quot; then you're right, what's the point of that in the story?<br /> <br /> If it's &quot;we've prophecied this baby will grow up to become the world's greatest monster so we should take him out now&quot; then it's more the moral question of to what extent should you do pre-emptive strikes, which is something that is actually a question people must face in real-life, only extended much further (since few people in real life know how dangerous someone is when they are a baby... though in the past with monarchies, it was a much more common moral question! Should you strangle this alternative to the throne who might well grow up to lead a brutal civil war of succession?).<br /> <br /> (It also lets Sidereals have slightly more freedom: they don't actually have to kill said baby, they just have to find a way to stop him growing up into the world's greatest monster. Killing him might be the easiest and most reliable way, but there are more difficult, but more moral alternatives. In the middle, kidnap him from his parents and take him to an orphanage on the other side of the world. More morally impeccable but a lot more effort, try to mould his life so he doesn't have the same bad influences. It makes for a story that might actually be interesting for Sidereal players. Not necessarily saying this is what Sidereal games should do every session, but it's a reasonable thing for them to be given as a minor mission perhaps.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-26-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:26:16-07:00","id":853536,"title":"","content":"This Sidereal's Great Prophecy thing, is it like classical prophecy that will definitely and magically come true no matter what you do, or is it more like people gathering data and then make a prediction that can turn out to be full of shit due to unaccountable factors ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853516#post853516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, the prophecy said that guiding the Solars out of their madness had a chance of success as well - the Bronze Faction basically decided that was a risk they couldn't take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohh, what I mean is whether the whole &quot;If the Sidereal don't kill the Solar, then Creation will definitely be destroyed&quot; thing is a setting fact said right there in the book or just a fanon thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 03-26-2016, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:36:13-07:00","id":853538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853536#post853536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Sidereal's Great Prophecy thing, is it like classical prophecy that will definitely and magically come true no matter what you do, or is it more like people gathering data and then make a prediction that can turn out to be full of shit due to unaccountable factors ?</div> </div> </div> </div>More the latter, really. The Great Prophecy is not intended to say &quot;the Path of Bronze was the objectively correct utilitarian thing to do,&quot; it's to say, &quot;the Sidereals largely saw two options, and one side won out.&quot;<br /> <br /> None of this was helped by the Sidereals' Great Curse of being myopic when working as a group. <br /> <br /> As to the former point, the accuracy of the Prophecy was always in question, and I think the point in myth is that the veracity of it coming true is always up in the air! Because prophecy is rarely described as absolute, and one has to wonder how often one makes a prophecy come true simply in taking actions to avoid it happening (see Oedipus - when you actively try to thwart a prophecy, such actions of avoidance are in fact the impetus for the prophecy actually being fulfilled).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853536#post853536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ohh, what I mean is whether the whole &quot;If the Sidereal don't kill the Solar, then Creation will definitely be destroyed&quot; thing is a setting fact said right there in the book or just a fanon thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know if it's a setting fact, because it never came to pass. We can only speak in hypotheticals.<br /> <br /> All that we can say is that the Sidereals certainly believed that to do nothing would be to destroy Creation, and one side of the argument--the &quot;kill them all&quot; side--simply won out. There are any number of reasons for why this group won, not the least being a notion that it might be easier to overthrow the Solars than to try to reform them from within, hubris and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T09:52:52-07:00","id":853544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853538#post853538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that we can say is that the Sidereals certainly believed that to do nothing would be to destroy Creation, and one side of the argument--the &quot;kill them all&quot; side--simply won out. There are any number of reasons for why this group won, not the least being a notion that it might be easier to overthrow the Solars than to try to reform them from within, hubris and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the last part of this is an often-overlooked factor in the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Because the Great Prophecy didn't occur in a vacuum. The Sidereals didn't decide to all band together and preform a singular working never done before and which probably can't be replicated again, at least, not in the same way for<i> fun.</i> They did that in the context of realizing &quot;holy shit, the Solars have turned into monsters, <i>we didn't see this coming and weren't prepared for it</i>. We're supposed to safeguard Creation from precisely this sort of bullshit, but usually how we react to crises of this nature is to tell the Solars and then help them deal with it, and that seems problematic for obvious reasons now. What the hell are we going to do?&quot;<br /> <br /> And in that context there's going to be a lot of pressure for actually resolving the immediate problem. The Usurpation was just as much about solving the problem Creation had <i>right then</i> as it was about preventing an awful apocalyptic future. Indeed, it might been the more salient; a potential apocalyptic future you can deal with as an abstract problem; the people who wield the Mandate becoming manifestly unworthy of it isn't abstract, it is happening right in front of you right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:26:47-07:00","id":853554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853538#post853538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that we can say is that the Sidereals certainly believed that to do nothing would be to destroy Creation, and one side of the argument--the &quot;kill them all&quot; side--simply won out. There are any number of reasons for why this group won, not the least being a notion that it might be easier to overthrow the Solars than to try to reform them from within, hubris and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and a willingness to murder the guys who didn't go along with the plan - that helps, yeah?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:38:57-07:00","id":853562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853528#post853528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's &quot;we've prophecied this baby will grow up to become the world's greatest monster so we should take him out now&quot; then it's more the moral question of to what extent should you do pre-emptive strikes, which is something that is actually a question people must face in real-life, only extended much further (since few people in real life know how dangerous someone is when they are a baby... though in the past with monarchies, it was a much more common moral question! Should you strangle this alternative to the throne who might well grow up to lead a brutal civil war of succession?).<br /> <br /> (It also lets Sidereals have slightly more freedom: they don't actually have to kill said baby, they just have to find a way to stop him growing up into the world's greatest monster. Killing him might be the easiest and most reliable way, but there are more difficult, but more moral alternatives. In the middle, kidnap him from his parents and take him to an orphanage on the other side of the world. More morally impeccable but a lot more effort, try to mould his life so he doesn't have the same bad influences. It makes for a story that might actually be interesting for Sidereal players. Not necessarily saying this is what Sidereal games should do every session, but it's a reasonable thing for them to be given as a minor mission perhaps.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's more fine. Although, for the specific example... history's greatest monster doesn't come up that often, Sidereal prediction doesn't seem to be generally that accurate in advance (Raken Thulio is still a thing, last time they checked, for one), killing full grown mortals doesn't seem that hard (and predicting Exalts is *really* not that possible, so what's the chances he'd Exalt?), etc. etc.<br /> <br /> But yes for more tractable and probable and proportionate versions of what is in spirit the same theme (i.e. things that are reasonable to suppose given the general accuracy of Heaven's foresight and not what is essentially Cabin In The Woods type bureaucratized propitiation of random dark forces behaviour).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853536#post853536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Sidereal's Great Prophecy thing, is it like classical prophecy that will definitely and magically come true no matter what you do, or is it more like people gathering data and then make a prediction that can turn out to be full of shit due to unaccountable factors ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a both schools of thought on this, and the books frankly don't really clear it up. Although I think the latter is probably more useful.<br /> <br /> (There's also the real-classy, have-cake-also-eat, third option where the Sidereals were wrong about all the upsides of a safer world from transferring rule to the Dragonblooded (because there's all this nasty stuff outside fate the Sidereals can't predict, so who knows if the world's *really* safer or not, right?), but were absolutely, infallibly, definitely, magically right about all the downsides of the Usurpation (inevitable loss of glory). Which, as an option, I can't see really ever had any point other than &quot;In your face Sidereals!&quot; but still annoys me to the point I take random, even off topic opportunities, like this one, to bemoan it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:51:46-07:00","id":853570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853554#post853554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and a willingness to murder the guys who didn't go along with the plan - that helps, yeah?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's notable that the proto-Bronze Faction understood exactly what they were up against, and this was the logical &quot;utilitarian&quot; response to people who were not going to be convinced, on the basis of OpSec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:06:03-07:00","id":856222,"title":"","content":"Another quick thought: what if the firmament of the Underworld is literally ghosts? Like once your business is finished and you move on to lethe, the aspects of your haunts become permanent fixtures that other ghosts can use. Thus the Deathlords and Deathknights have some invested interest in helping ghosts pass on in the long term.<br /> <br /> Also, it would make ghosts a coveted commodity in the Underworld, as they are necessary ingredient for expanding or improving your holdings. Maybe the Deathlords even make a tidy business in trading them? Only the lower souls in more benevolent domains of course. Did anyone besides me read Tom Judge? The Hell in that world worked upon a similar principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:30:13-07:00","id":856236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853536#post853536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Sidereal's Great Prophecy thing, is it like classical prophecy that will definitely and magically come true no matter what you do, or is it more like people gathering data and then make a prediction that can turn out to be full of shit due to unaccountable factors ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ohh, what I mean is whether the whole &quot;If the Sidereal don't kill the Solar, then Creation will definitely be destroyed&quot; thing is a setting fact said right there in the book or just a fanon thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>During 2E there was a point some people who didn't like the Sids latched on to. Three things are notably outside of Fate and so not included in prophecy: Demons, Dead, and creatures of the Wyld. Given that those were also three for three in greatest threats to the world it seems like the Sids appeared to have ignored the most glaringly obvious reason their prophecy was worthless in the long term. Consequently they didn't and couldn't predict the Great Contagion or the Balorian Crusade, any assurances of safety were empty, and Creation was saved by pure luck when the Empress got control of the Imperial Manse.<br /> <br /> On explanation for that was getting all those Sids together made their curse worse and they couldn't admit that there were glaring holes in their prophetic ability. This has the side effect of making the Usurpation have some of the worst possible justification while not making it entirely unnecessary since in the short term the Solars really were a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T17:00:14-07:00","id":856778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=856222#post856222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another quick thought: what if the firmament of the Underworld is literally ghosts? Like once your business is finished and you move on to lethe, the aspects of your haunts become permanent fixtures that other ghosts can use. Thus the Deathlords and Deathknights have some invested interest in helping ghosts pass on in the long term.<br /> <br /> Also, it would make ghosts a coveted commodity in the Underworld, as they are necessary ingredient for expanding or improving your holdings. Maybe the Deathlords even make a tidy business in trading them? Only the lower souls in more benevolent domains of course. Did anyone besides me read Tom Judge? The Hell in that world worked upon a similar principle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Valuing ghosts as commodities sounds like it'd devalue them as <i>characters</i>.<br /> <br /> It's why I didn't enjoy 2e's Sidereals &quot;mining&quot; gods for starmetal, Deathlords soulforging ghosts by the thousands, or Infernals rendering demons down into energy drinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:55:40-07:00","id":866533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852567#post852567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esoteric metaphysical justification for concretely bad behavior always strikes me as weaksauce bullshit whenever fantasy fiction authors invoke it for why their bad boys aren't <i>actually</i> bad after all and so the audience doesn't have to feel guilty for liking them. And that's what this sort of thing always amounts to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just recently, I was thinking about this <i>My Little Pony</i> fanfic I had the misfortune to either read or hear a detailed account about.<br /> <br /> In this story, alicorns fueled their immortality by swallowing and digesting lesser ponies whole, alive, and <i>awake</i>. Celestia was urging the newly-alicorn Twilight to eat a trembling Applejack, who was bribed into accepting this horrible death by Celestia promising to financially support Applejack's family and farm for a few generations.<br /> <br /> But really, it's just the author wanting to write a story in which people EAT OTHER PEOPLE ALIVE and he doesn't have to feel guilty about it, because the alicorns need to stay immortal for the good of Equestria, and these victims are totally volunteers!<br /> <br /> Bullshit. Ugly, ugly bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:47:49-07:00","id":866550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=852595#post852595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;For the greater good&quot; in that sense and embraced wholeheartedly is and always has been satire. There's a reason why it's best known from Warhammer 40k and Hot Fuzz. Also, moving the Deathlords from &quot;Servants of the Neverborn&quot; to &quot;Free actors who stole power from the Neverborn&quot; does not move them from selfish to altruistic without significantly more alteration necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this include Sidereals?<br /> <br /> I'm half-serious. Lately, the more I thought about the Usurpation and the way Exalted presents it, the more it bothers me. In-setting, it works; there's this prophecy and the Sidereals finally, sorrowfully decide that the only way to save the world is to nearly destroy it and take control of its future themselves. They don't <i>want</i> to do this -- ruling the world from behind the scenes is so very much work! Their books make clear just how much painful work it is to run the world from behind the scenes, how stretched-thin they are; surely they wouldn't have done this if they didn't absolutely have to! Why, Kejak cried for an entire day after nearly destroying civilization in order to seize power. An entire day!<br /> <br /> The problem I have with it is that this is exactly the sort of thing people who lead real-world coups say. &quot;I didn't want to do it, but I had to to save the country, and look at how much painful work it is; I don't really <i>enjoy</i> leading, I've been forced into it...&quot; is the kind of thing I'd have expected out of, say, Muammar Gaddafi.<br /> <br /> (Their continued inability to make any sort of peace with the Lunars is also extremely questionable when viewed from this light -- sure, the Lunars are really really angry, but at the end of the day the Sidereals have spent the last 1500 years killmurdering anyone who could oppose their grip on Creation's future, explicitly including people who have no particular place in their great prophecy. I'm increasingly uncomfortable with the way the book tries to justify that or to say how ruling Creation from behind the scenes is <i>so hard</i>.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:50:06-07:00","id":866571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866550#post866550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this include Sidereals?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bronze Faction were obviously intended to be bad guys but the Solars keep drowning in designated protagonist crap like the idea that the Dragon-Blooded used to be slaves and should be 100% happy going back to this because that's the natural order.<br /> <br /> Edit: to clarify that's still ultimately a problem with the 1e Sidereals book, the lack of Dragon-Blooded rights in Yu-Shan really highlights and underscores their place in the First Age and if you're willing to excuse that for metaphysical reasons, where do you draw the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-16-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T18:21:18-07:00","id":866593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=853099#post853099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Oblivion is that it tries to reshift the focus of the entire game. It sends the message that the battles over the Realm and the like don't really matter compared to this inevitable world-destroying force at the root of the world that must be confronted.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> I've mentioned this with regards to Infernals, but it affected Abyssals, too... I think that if you look at, say, your typical Final Fantasy game, there's a moment when the game is done introducing you to the world and says &quot;all right, now you're going to fight a superdemon.&quot; And from then on the story is all about killing a monster clown or an evil tree or a Sephiroth or whatever, and the other stuff stops mattering so much. And I think that because that kind of storytelling has become so widespread in videogames, people expect it out of Exalted. But I also think it's really really bad for a tabletop game, since it means you're discarding most of what matters to the main game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something touched on in this video, &quot;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=35P_9MgxlQU\" target=\"_blank\">The Philosophy of Final Fantasy</a>&quot;.<br /> <br /> After watching that video, I immediately felt <i>cheated </i>by Squaresoft. I wondered what kind of stories could have been told if...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Final Fantasy plot-twists below:</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">...in <i>Final Fantasy 6</i>, Emperor Gestahl had possessed enough sense to know Kefka was a mad dog and thus held him on a tight enough leash that Kefka DIDN'T murder General Leo, DIDN'T throw the Emperor off the floating continent, and DIDN'T destroy the world and become a god of destruction.<br /> <br /> What if the rest of the story in <i>Final Fantasy 6</i> was dealing with the fact that the Empire now had the powers of the goddesses, on top of controlling most of the planet? The Emperor and even the honorable General Leo would still be your enemies. Leo could be confronted about the evil he was agreeing to commit in the name of national loyalty. The Emperor would still be engaging in the story of nations, industrialization, invasion, occupation, and exploitation.<br /> <br /> What if Sephiroth had never shown his whiny-ass face? What if the rest of the story of<i> Final Fantasy 7</i> was about continuing the fight against the Shinra Corporation, quite possibly with the ORIGINAL Mr. Shinra in charge (since Sephiroth didn't show up to conveniently murder him for you) and his son Rufus agitating in the corner.<br /> <br /> What if Kuja had never gotten the chance to throw his genocidal hissy-fit, so that the rest of <i>Final Fantasy 9 </i>would have been actually dealing with an entire other world of people that wanted to invade and conquer? OR, even earlier than them, what if the story was still dealing with that butt-ugly queen who wanted to conquer the world even when it meant destroying entire kingdoms and endangering whole sapient species of people?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All of these complex stories and their possible messages and lessons were always tossed out the window so that you could have a simple, purely evil villain to punch in the face until the world was saved. If that's what Final Fantasy was going to be about, then maybe they could have left all of the complexity out of the beginnings so that we could just cut to the fucking chase?<br /> <br /> Like, I think <i>Kingdom Hearts</i> might pretty much be the clean distillation of a <i>Final Fantasy</i> game, in that light. &quot;Simple and Clean&quot;, if you will.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel <i>Chrono Trigger</i> struck the best balance, actually. Even though you get briefly stuck into the historic past of the Human/Mystic war before learning about Lavos, there was never the sense that you personally needed to worry about that war. Because in the modern day, the war is long over, and the humans (which includes you) won. All you care about is rescuing Marle, which you do before learning about Lavos.<br /> <br /> Even after learning about Lavos, you're continuously introduced to various smaller stories that have little or nothing to do with dealing with Lavos, and none of them feel meaningless! Because you're always engaged and bound up in these smaller stories.<br /> <br /> I think, maybe, there's this sense of &quot;sure, we've got to save the world from dying -- but we also care about making a world that's worth LIVING in&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-16-2016, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T18:59:45-07:00","id":866602,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. One thing I really love about the <i>Suikoden</i> series (especially 1 and 2) is that it avoided the urge to replace its story about warfare and society and <i>people</i> with some bullshit magical supergod.<br /> <br /> If Squaresoft had written Suikoden II, Luca Blight would have gotten some supergod power halfway through and the nations and wars would have stopped mattering. Instead, by having the war continue after his death, it made it clear that the nations and the conflict involved were bigger than any one person -- it made them the main focus. Even if Luca Blight was a fun character, it wouldn't have been as good of a game if they had made the last act focus on how evil and superpowerful he was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T19:01:32-07:00","id":866603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866571#post866571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bronze Faction were obviously intended to be bad guys but the Solars keep drowning in designated protagonist crap like the idea that the Dragon-Blooded used to be slaves and should be 100% happy going back to this because that's the natural order.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the only canonical Solar who is <i>really</i> like that is Lyta, and she's hardly a sympathetic character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T19:40:14-07:00","id":866618,"title":"","content":"Guys, guys, spoilers! I'm just playing FF9 now for the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:03:51-07:00","id":866627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866603#post866603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the only canonical Solar who is <i>really</i> like that is Lyta, and she's hardly a sympathetic character.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much how individual Solars behave so much as setting creep about what it means to be a Solar, the Unconquered Sun\u2019s semi-regular characterisation as a paranoid dictator and by extension a sense that history is just going to repeat itself.<br /> <br /> I can see how someone working from 2e especially can enjoy their Solars, their friends Solars but remain sympathetic to the argument that the Solars as a whole represent a danger to Creation. A lot of this is bad canon like the the Solar Bond or the Mandate of Heaven but it still shapes perceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-17-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:14:51-07:00","id":866630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866618#post866618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, guys, spoilers! I'm just playing FF9 now for the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Darth Vader is Luke's father.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I AM sorry that I spoiled something for you, so as a kindness to anyone else who might not have played these games in the last ten (or 15?) years, I have placed the plot twists under spoiler tags.<br /> <br /> ...Wait, why didn't you stop reading at FF7? Couldn't you guess I was going to mention 8 or 9 next?<br /> <br /> I skipped 8 because I just didn't give a shit about it, but I mentioned Kuja by name at the start of the sentence in the passage where I'm throwing out ALL The Spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-16-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:26:58-07:00","id":866637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866630#post866630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevertheless, I AM sorry that I spoiled something for you, so as a kindness to anyone else who might not have played these games in the last ten (or 15?) years, I have placed the plot twists under spoiler tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>Final Fantasy IX has apparently only just recently been released on Steam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T20:31:06-07:00","id":866638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866637#post866637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Final Fantasy IX has apparently only just recently been released on Steam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That makes sense.<br /> <br /> I might actually get to play it now!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T21:09:15-07:00","id":866653,"title":"","content":"I was kidding, I stopped reading as soon as you got to 9.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, last year I watched Star Wars with a girl who'd never, ever seen it. Her reaction to finding out about Luke's father was &quot;What, really? Is he lying? Surely he's lying.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-17-2016, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T21:15:51-07:00","id":866654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866653#post866653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was kidding, I stopped reading as soon as you got to 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good. I am sincerely relieved. And even happier to have put those things under spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T21:31:04-07:00","id":866659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866550#post866550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this include Sidereals?<br /> <br /> I'm half-serious. Lately, the more I thought about the Usurpation and the way Exalted presents it, the more it bothers me. In-setting, it works; there's this prophecy and the Sidereals finally, sorrowfully decide that the only way to save the world is to nearly destroy it and take control of its future themselves. They don't <i>want</i> to do this -- ruling the world from behind the scenes is so very much work! Their books make clear just how much painful work it is to run the world from behind the scenes, how stretched-thin they are; surely they wouldn't have done this if they didn't absolutely have to! Why, Kejak cried for an entire day after nearly destroying civilization in order to seize power. An entire day!<br /> <br /> The problem I have with it is that this is exactly the sort of thing people who lead real-world coups say. &quot;I didn't want to do it, but I had to to save the country, and look at how much painful work it is; I don't really <i>enjoy</i> leading, I've been forced into it...&quot; is the kind of thing I'd have expected out of, say, Muammar Gaddafi.<br /> <br /> (Their continued inability to make any sort of peace with the Lunars is also extremely questionable when viewed from this light -- sure, the Lunars are really really angry, but at the end of the day the Sidereals have spent the last 1500 years killmurdering anyone who could oppose their grip on Creation's future, explicitly including people who have no particular place in their great prophecy. I'm increasingly uncomfortable with the way the book tries to justify that or to say how ruling Creation from behind the scenes is <i>so hard</i>.)</div> </div> </div> </div>But the book never specific whether the Great Prophecy is actually &quot;Mythological and Inescapable prophecy&quot; or just Sidereal seeing supper scary visions. So Kejak could be &quot;Hard man making hard decision&quot; or a chicken little either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:08:42-07:00","id":866672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866659#post866659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the book never specific whether the Great Prophecy is actually &quot;Mythological and Inescapable prophecy&quot; or just Sidereal seeing supper scary visions. So Kejak could be &quot;Hard man making hard decision&quot; or a chicken little either way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that is why I really dislike that character in particular. I LOATHE the whole &quot;hard man making the hard decisions&quot; thing you see in say... The Walking Dead or whatever. That said, I would happily welcome a presentation of him that I could like. Hell, I did the same with Peleps Deled.<br /> <br /> Anyways, back to the topic... I look back at previous editions of Exalted and start to think which splats just... never felt &quot;good&quot; to play. Lunars, Abyssals for me. Playing The Division (as problematic as it can be, has good points) is a perfect example. The &quot;bad guys&quot; are shown to have some real humanity and I felt BAD about taking them down. A friend actually was a bit choked up on finding a teddy bear on a merc's bed and a stuffed rabbit toy on another's. In the end, Exalted ARE human. They might be scary smart, strong, clever, etc... but their origins and therefore the things that shaped them, are that of a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T22:43:13-07:00","id":866684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866659#post866659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the book never specific whether the Great Prophecy is actually &quot;Mythological and Inescapable prophecy&quot; or just Sidereal seeing supper scary visions. So Kejak could be &quot;Hard man making hard decision&quot; or a chicken little either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2E it implicitly did because Fate was a scam. Destiny is the plan the celestial bureaucrats have for what they have decided is going to happen. Anyone important, or large expenditures of essence throw the whole thing out of whack. For the most part it was a fairly good indicator of future events because the people who drew up the plans were good and projecting trends and most people live boring predictable lives.<br /> <br /> They had to invent Samsara, or super Fate, to have the inescapable prophecy thing for all the true oracles to draw on. PCs could still give it the middle finger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:13:54-07:00","id":866690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866672#post866672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is why I really dislike that character in particular. I LOATHE the whole &quot;hard man making the hard decisions&quot; thing you see in say... The Walking Dead or whatever. That said, I would happily welcome a presentation of him that I could like. Hell, I did the same with Peleps Deled.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be part of my problem with it.<br /> <br /> I feel that in real life, when people invoke the &quot;hard man making the hard decisions&quot; argument, it's often people using it to defend indefensible things they wanted to do anyway. I compared Kejak to Muammar Gaddafi above; I wasn't entirely joking. Gaddafi is what I picture most &quot;hard men making hard decisions&quot; as being when you cut through their self-justifications. I am <i>extremely</i> skeptical about anyone who claims that they needed to seize power for the greater good; that is to say, absent evidence to the contrary, I would usually automatically assume that anyone who claims that is actually seizing power because they like to have power. And I'm particularly bothered by the default defense the Sidereals books seem to employ for this (&quot;are you kidding? Ruling the world is <i>hard</i> and painful and brings them no pleasure, but they do it for the <i>greater good</i>&quot;), because, again, that's exactly the line real-world people like Gaddafi trot out. I'm sure Sidereals have a lot of work to do, but they're doing it from gold-lined palaces in literal Heaven while they decide the fate of the entire world with their decisions. If they think they have things rough, hey, they could swap places with the Lunars any time they want! Nothing stops a Sidereal from walking out the door, giving up their temporal power and prestige and so on.<br /> <br /> Some of what they do is literally necessary, but a lot of it, like everything to do with guiding and supporting the Realm, say, is not. Except without the DB / Sidereal hegemony the world would be in chaos and anarchy and unlead and etc etc etc because of course having the firm hand of the Exalted guiding the world is <i>necessary</i>... ugh. Some of the common viewpoints on Exalted have issues when you look at them too closely, and not just regarding the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm only half-serious. Sidereals are playable and the Bronze Faction is meant to be at least somewhat sympathetic, so having Kejak be, canonically, Literally Gaddafi is not good for the game. But &quot;they wanted to seize power for the greater good&quot; and &quot;they wanted to seize power because they wanted power&quot; are not incompatible. In fact, the second follows inevitably from the first. I would imagine that long before the Usurpation, there was a faction of Sidereals that felt that they could use their understanding of Fate to guide the world more directly to better ends if they were the only ones in charge... and I would assume that this faction served as the core of what would eventually become the Bronze Faction.<br /> <br /> (If you assume there was a faction of Sidereals that had &quot;things would be better if we, who understand Fate the best, were the ones who were ultimately in charge&quot; even <i>before</i> the Great Prophecy, and that this formed the core of the Bronze Faction, this also explains why the Sidereals have failed to make any sort of peace with the Lunars over the past 1500 years. I would assume that not all Sidereals, even in the Bronze Faction, are part of this Sidereal Supremacy faction, but the history of Creation makes a lot more sense if you posit that it exists. This doesn't mean that they don't want peace, but if you assume that there's this hard core of the Bronze Faction whose ideology states that Sidereals should be in charge and that Creation should be run according to their understanding of fate, then they are always going to be structurally incapable of making any sort of lasting peace with other Celestial Exalted.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not so much how individual Solars behave so much as setting creep about what it means to be a Solar, the Unconquered Sun\u2019s semi-regular characterisation as a paranoid dictator and by extension a sense that history is just going to repeat itself.<br /> <br /> I can see how someone working from 2e especially can enjoy their Solars, their friends Solars but remain sympathetic to the argument that the Solars as a whole represent a danger to Creation. </div> </div> </div>Oh, Solars <i>definitely</i> pose a danger to Creation. I'm just bothered by the basic shape of the story. I don't think there's any way to avoid the problem or to fix it; you can't present Kejak Chejop as Literally Gaddafi. If you poke at the heroic narrative too closely from a more cynical modern viewpoint, it all falls apart. That's obviously not limited to Sidereals.<br /> <br /> But... I'm still bothered by how the Bronze Faction is portrayed and by the fact that accepting the story requires, on some level, that we accept their statement that they were at least <i>motivated</i> by the greater good. This is necessary for Exalted to tell the kind of story that it wants to tell, but it also has some nasty implications if you look at it too closely, because if we were discussing anything in the real world remotely analogous to that story, I would be extremely skeptical, not just about whether they made the right decision but about whether their motivations were really what they say they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-17-2016, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:26:04-07:00","id":866695,"title":"","content":"There's always the option that, like many politicians, they went in with good intentions, but when you hang out exclusively with people who's other Ferrari is a Bemtly and their other other Ferrari is a G5, your perspective changes a lot. Or you might start out wanting to start a revolution to guide a Solar rebellion into tearing down the Realm and putting the Solars back in their place of ruling the world, but then you get used to being able able to control the immaculate order, the imperial navy, and the thousand scales....and you realize that this level of control would be impossible if you were trying to assert it over Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:31:13-07:00","id":866696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But... I'm still bothered by how the Bronze Faction is portrayed and by the fact that accepting the story requires, on some level, that we accept their statement that they were at least <i>motivated</i> by the greater good. This is necessary for Exalted to tell the kind of story that it wants to tell, but it also has some nasty implications if you look at it too closely, because if we were discussing anything in the real world remotely analogous to that story, I would be extremely skeptical, not just about whether they made the right decision but about whether their motivations were really what they say they were. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that's the point. They believe themselves to be motivated by the greater good, claim to be, etc, but the characters don't have to accept this. The Lunar PC in my game had pretty much this exact argument when he met the ghost of Chejop Kejak.<br /> <br /> Just as, in real life, there are dictators who flat-out just care about having a good life for them and their families, but there are other dictators who convince themselves that they are acting for the greater good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T23:46:04-07:00","id":866698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866533#post866533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, it's just the author wanting to write a story in which people EAT OTHER PEOPLE ALIVE and he doesn't have to feel guilty about it, because the alicorns need to stay immortal for the good of Equestria, and these victims are totally volunteers!<br /> <br /> Bullshit. Ugly, ugly bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read this particular fic, but I think the point would be that the benefits of the atrocity are <i>debatable</i>, not absolute. Moral choices are only interesting, from a writing perspective, if you can conceivably imagine a situation where both options are the right one. It sounds like this story could have done a better job playing devil's advocate, but the idea that Applejack is a <i>willing</i> participant at least adds one element that might make readers stop and consider the situation before decrying the Alicorns and their pony-sacrifice.<br /> <br /> I was actually just talking about another story, Dragon Age Inquisition, that does a pretty good job posing these moral quandaries:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Iron Bull's Decision: Iron Bull is a loyal follower of the Qun, a religious/social order that has dictated his every major life decision since birth. Operating as one of their spies, he begins leading a small mercenary band called &quot;the Chargers&quot; which the player gets to meet and develop attachments towards. Eventually though the Qun come calling. They need Iron Bull's Chargers to serve as a distraction for one of their warships, which has over one hundred soldiers on board. You the player then have to decide whether to (A) save these six mercenaries that you know and love, or (B) save one hundred faceless soldiers that might potentially help you save the world.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What is most interesting about this example is that <i>most</i> people I talk to think that option &quot;A&quot; is the &quot;right&quot; choice, and would have very nasty things to say about those who chose option &quot;B.&quot; But a person motivated by altruism might reasonably pick either choice, and we wouldn't conclusively be able to say they were right or wrong in doing so. That to me is the benchmark for a well-written moral quandary, a benchmark Ex2 Abyssals fail miserably because at no point do any of the books even attempt to make a compelling case that Oblivion is preferable to life.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation fairs slightly better in that regard: at least a few of the Sidereals might reasonably be assumed to be operating on altruism and a sincere belief that the Solars were nutso-crazy-banana-town (because many were), though with what we know out of character about their Great Curse and the functional limits of Fate it seems very unlikely that this was true for all of them. And ultimately, it is very hard to empathize with the victor of a bloody military coup, no matter what their intentions were.<br /> <br /> But good intentions that don't produce the desired result are a cornerstone of Exalted storytelling. All I'm hoping to inject into the Abyssal splat here is the same moral latitude the other Exalted have to be good or evil depending on player choice, instead of being pigeon-holed into the bad guy role because their exaltations are inescapably tied to a mission statement no good or sane person would support. You are of course well within your rights to say that no goal is worth torturing and killing millions of people over, but I am within my rights also to say that &quot;one is less than many, and many is less than all,&quot; which I think is pretty solid ground to stand on when writing gothic horror anti-heroes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Another great story where the bad guys are pretty damn bad but not entirely irredeemable: Cabin in the Woods. In fact, that entire movie could serve as source material for a loyalist Abyssal game in my proposed setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 04-17-2016, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T00:08:41-07:00","id":866703,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a>, you're questioning the logic in someone's porno. No, in fact, most pizza delivery guys <i>don't</i> get into protracted sexual misadventures with their customers, and ponies in a kids' show about how the bonds of friendship can overcome all other forces won't casually break those bonds to murder one another with their gastric juices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T00:35:33-07:00","id":866710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866703#post866703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a>, you're questioning the logic in someone's porno. No, in fact, most pizza delivery guys <i>don't</i> get into protracted sexual misadventures with their customers, and ponies in a kids' show about how the bonds of friendship can overcome all other forces won't casually break those bonds to murder one another with their gastric juices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to say, yeah, that read to me like a description of some sort of fetish-oriented fic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T00:59:33-07:00","id":866715,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that I've not even shared some of the other reasons a Deathknight would be this kind of a loyalist, besides the &quot;ends justify the means&quot; argument. Here are a few:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Underworld is our home, and Creation stands against us.&quot; Many Abyssals had close ties to the Underworld before their exaltation, and care deeply for the people there. Creation might have been your home at one point, but now its people are alien and hostile to you. The ancestor cults that keep your loved ones alive are persecuted by the living, who would like nothing better than for you and your ilk to disappear forever. If a few or many of these enemies have to die painful deaths so that your friends and family can enjoy their peaceful lives for many, many years more, then so be it.<br /> <br /> &quot;We <i>can</i> have nice things.&quot; Everything in the Underworld is the phantom image of something in Creation that got there by dying. Even the landscapes are only memories made real by the ghosts who come here. So if you want something, <i>anything</i> really, and it doesn't already exist in the Underworld, then that is categorically going to require somebody to die. Sure, you could all &quot;get by&quot; without killing Bob the farmer, but how happy is everyone going to be when his apple orchards start filling the local markets with fresh produce? The living kill people for stuff all the time, but when we kill someone we make sure <i>everyone</i> benefits for <i>centuries.<br /> <br /> &quot;</i>They'll be happier as ghosts.&quot; Not existing is a terrible choice. But between rotting, painful flesh sacks and untiring, un-aging ectoplasm, many would choose the latter. Being a ghost is not without downsides, of course, but you'll never have to worry about a whole host of things you did in life, your friends and family are always nearby, you'll finally have time to catch up on your reading, and if your Abyssal patron is kind you can expect to be well taken care of after only a brief period of intense discomfort. It's more of an early retirement plan, really.<br /> <br /> &quot;Some people deserve it.&quot; No one ever said you had to kill indiscriminately to meet those ghost quotas. There are plenty of objectively awful, evil people alive in Creation right now and you can easily keep Oblivion at bay without ever shedding innocent blood. Whether you have a personal vendetta against rapist, sadists, child abusers, career criminals or politcal tyrants that mortal laws can't touch, your Second Breath has given you all the power you need to bring these scumbags to justice and protect innocent un-lives doing it. And once they're in ghost-prison you can lock them up and throw away the key for eternity, because undead justice never takes a day off.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's always a party in Halloween Town.&quot; Making a ghost requires a special mix of negative emotions, strong sentiments and unfinished business that is impossible to mass-produce. Every ghost is made-to-order and you're an expert when it comes to brewing that miserable ectoplasmic cocktail, but you haven't killed a single person since your Second Breath and you don't plan to. You're too busy arranging midnight hauntings, terrible nightmares and tailored psychological traumas to get your own hands dirty, and the dangers of the Second Age pretty much guarantee that the last step in ghost production always gets done with or without your help. Not all your clients appreciate the work you put in, but there's nothing half as satisfying as a blood-curdling scream that you made yourself!<br /> <br /> &quot;It won't always be like this.&quot; The Deathlords know that the current system is cruel, and they wish it didn't have to be. Oblivion is by its very nature hazardous to study, and is barely understood even by its most devoted experts. You are continuously researching better, less destructive weapons in the fight against Oblivion, and one day soon your efforts will bear fruit and the Underworld and Creation will be able to live in harmony as they always should. But no one is going to live to see that better tomorrow unless you knuckle down and bring us a bag of dead kittens, so get to work, Deathknight.<br /> <br /> ...to name a few.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T02:20:22-07:00","id":866727,"title":"","content":"These mostly (not sure about the last) seem like good motivations for an Abyssal generally. I don't really see them as being part of a plan to subvert Oblivion though, they're just independent of it.<br /> Which is, in my opinion, a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T02:33:45-07:00","id":866732,"title":"","content":"To be honest, if the Usurpation &quot;hard choice&quot; really felt like a big issue, I would be more tempted to make Sidereals more like Hari Seldon and the Foundation that was part of their inspiration. <br /> Seldon's psychohistory allowed him to predict the fall of the Galactic Empire, but he wasn't making any decision other than to set up his Foundations.<br /> <br /> The Fall of the First Age could go the same way - the Sidereals did not cause the Usurpation, but foresaw it, and planned for it, out of both altruism and more self interested motives, as an opportunity to gain the reins of history, and chose not to intervene to spread awareness, viewing the Solar regime as ultimately unworthy of that chance, an act for which the Lunars still blame them.<br /> <br /> Parenthetically, you really need to avoid the Sidereals and Dragonblooded becoming just part of a Solars' &quot;revenge movie&quot; plot, where it's simply the case that &quot;We were robbed of our rightful place, by the usurpers who had no justification than greed and we are back to claim it&quot;. And then from there just playing out like any tired revenge flick like The Revenant, anything like that. My view of the core Solar story is that, for most games, it's meant to be about it slowly dawning on the reborn Solars, as they find their way in the world that, &quot;Shit. We really screwed up last time. How are we not going to make the same mistakes again? Is this our fate? Can we really be trusted with any power? Should any man be? Do I really have the ultimate right to make these decisions, that I feel I must make?&quot;. A story with strong elements of the humbling and the self doubting, trying to wield power justly while doubting to a degree whether you should wield it at all, not a total story of revenge and self belief. (Although of course there are many, many Solars who don't quite fit that template.). So you can't take away responsibility for the Usurpation and you can't make it a wholly unjust wrong against them, or you step all over that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T03:56:09-07:00","id":866745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866593#post866593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After watching that video, I immediately felt <i>cheated </i>by Squaresoft. I wondered what kind of stories could have been told if...<br /> <br /> <b>Final Fantasy plot-twists below:</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">...in <i>Final Fantasy 6</i>, Emperor Gestahl had possessed enough sense to know Kefka was a mad dog and thus held him on a tight enough leash that Kefka DIDN'T murder General Leo, DIDN'T throw the Emperor off the floating continent, and DIDN'T destroy the world and become a god of destruction.<br /> <br /> What if the rest of the story in <i>Final Fantasy 6</i> was dealing with the fact that the Empire now had the powers of the goddesses, on top of controlling most of the planet? The Emperor and even the honorable General Leo would still be your enemies. Leo could be confronted about the evil he was agreeing to commit in the name of national loyalty. The Emperor would still be engaging in the story of nations, industrialization, invasion, occupation, and exploitation.<br /> <br /> What if Sephiroth had never shown his whiny-ass face? What if the rest of the story of<i> Final Fantasy 7</i> was about continuing the fight against the Shinra Corporation, quite possibly with the ORIGINAL Mr. Shinra in charge (since Sephiroth didn't show up to conveniently murder him for you) and his son Rufus agitating in the corner.<br /> <br /> What if Kuja had never gotten the chance to throw his genocidal hissy-fit, so that the rest of <i>Final Fantasy 9 </i>would have been actually dealing with an entire other world of people that wanted to invade and conquer? OR, even earlier than them, what if the story was still dealing with that butt-ugly queen who wanted to conquer the world even when it meant destroying entire kingdoms and endangering whole sapient species of people?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All of these complex stories and their possible messages and lessons were always tossed out the window so that you could have a simple, purely evil villain to punch in the face until the world was saved. If that's what Final Fantasy was going to be about, then maybe they could have left all of the complexity out of the beginnings so that we could just cut to the fucking chase.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a sort of mixed feeling about that.<br /> <br /> On the one hand...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">that's a pretty unique reaction though. I don't know if many people really ever really started FF7 and though &quot;This game is going to be all about fighting the Shinra Corporation, until the end, and the gameplay is going to be about organising increasingly successful rebel actions and then working out how to actually govern things in the aftermath&quot;. Or would feel that way after the fact. You fight increasingly powerful, strange bosses with a small team, and explore your team's developing small scale personal scale relationships and history, and the tone is generally pretty light. <br /> <br /> It's not, like, the game is introduced as a strategy game or a game where it's like Fallout where you're making kind of weighty choices between political factions. I don't know if I see a whole lot of complexity in the Gesthal Empire, or Shinra, the Galbadian Dictatorship, or Alexandria or the Church of Yevon, specifically, that is swept aside. I don't feel like I was champing at the bit to find out more about who the people were in these groups, and how they justified to themselves what they did, and whether they could be allies or had to be opponents and so on. That's not really where any focus felt like it could be.<br /> <br /> (A separate note, is, even on its own terms, for example for FF6 you could also say it would have been just as interesting to deal with the political aftermath of Kefka's destruction of the world. What new powers form in the apocalyptic aftermath? What is the Cult of Ruin, exactly? How is this all informed by the world that came before? Rather than seeing that as a detracting shift.) </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> On the other hand, I can see the appeal of a videogame that had the kind of iconic artistry in character design, world design, monsters, art, music, scenario, mood as a classic Final Fantasy game, with the kind of choice and complicated politics and large scale strategy found in other videogames. It's a big ask though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T05:52:28-07:00","id":866772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866745#post866745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a sort of mixed feeling about that.<br /> <br /> On the one hand...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">that's a pretty unique reaction though. I don't know if many people really ever really started FF7 and though &quot;This game is going to be all about fighting the Shinra Corporation, until the end, and the gameplay is going to be about organising increasingly successful rebel actions and then working out how to actually govern things in the aftermath&quot;. Or would feel that way after the fact. You fight increasingly powerful, strange bosses with a small team, and explore your team's developing small scale personal scale relationships and history, and the tone is generally pretty light.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>(FF7 + FF5 spoilers.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I totally did think that, no joking. I mean, I didn't think I'd <i>control</i> it or make those choices, but I thought the plot would be primarily about fighting Shinra. I went into the game without being spoiled on it at all, and my reaction for most of the second half of the first disk was &quot;when is this sideplot about chasing around a black-cloaked man going to end so we can get back to fighting Shinra?&quot;<br /> <br /> I have no idea why people think Sephiroth is an interesting character. Hell, I have no idea why people think he <i>is</i> a character, he has like three lines. Does he even say anything in the last part of the game when you fight him? I don't think he does. I'm not sure he's still even sentient at that point. Honestly I'm not sure he was sentient at any point after being killed and falling into the lifestream, he was just sort of an... echo-thing? It wasn't very clear. My reading is that he didn't actually manage to resurrect completely, it's just that some sort of echos of him possessed people. But it felt like an entirely valid interpretation that at no point during actual gameplay was there an actual, awake, thinking Sephiroth; he died years ago and every time you saw him, it was just mindless echos of him that occasionally took over people who shared his genes or whatever the hell it was. As I recall, even after he theoretically reassembles himself, he doesn't have a single line in the &quot;real world&quot; as opposed to in people's heads.<br /> <br /> I could be forgetting something? But I'm pretty sure he never does or says anything that would imply that he's sentient in the modern day, or in any way cognizant of what's happening outside of a few reflexive instincts to attack certain people and grab / use certain things. Like, seriously, Exdeath was a less wooden character, and he was <i>literally a tree</i>.<br /> <br /> But more generally, I felt that Midgar was the only remotely interesting or fleshed-out location in the game. None of the scenes set outside of Midgar were remotely as effective to me as the ones inside it because of that; the rest of the world was pretty much just generic Final Fantasy places.<br /> <br /> (I have other issues regarding it being about your character's relationships, though. I felt that that its development of those collapsed after you left Midgar the first time and were able to select your party; from that point on, there was almost no interaction between anyone in your party and anyone except Cloud. This is common, but it's still irritating. The only characters who get any real characterization outside of their one designated sidequest are Cloud, Aeris, Tifa, and Barret, and most of that is in the early game when they knew who would be in your party. I replayed the game recently and it was <i>extremely noticeable</i> how the density of characterization and plot collapsed, sharply, after you left Midgar, replaced with long stretches of just going from place to place. But this is a bit off-topic, because that issue doesn't really have much to do with Exalted or tabletop games in general. Still, it annoys me how many games fall into that trap where the characterization suddenly stops or slows to a crawl once you can control who's in your party... or just adding tons of characters at the expense of fleshing them out.)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-17-2016, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T06:15:47-07:00","id":866782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866690#post866690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Solars <i>definitely</i> pose a danger to Creation. I'm just bothered by the basic shape of the story. I don't think there's any way to avoid the problem or to fix it; you can't present Kejak Chejop as Literally Gaddafi. If you poke at the heroic narrative too closely from a more cynical modern viewpoint, it all falls apart. That's obviously not limited to Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well with Solars it's mostly a matter of avoiding them coming across as cosmic trust fund babies and 3e has already taken some pretty significant steps away from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T06:15:59-07:00","id":866783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/851941-what-if-abyssals-were-fighting-oblivion-all-along?p=866772#post866772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(FF7 + FF5 spoilers.)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div sty